window.SST_UNIFIED_DATA = {"S001":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Now, the study of biology is responsible for some of the most profound insights that humans have, about the world around them. So, take a look at these four panoramas. In the upper left, you see some bacteria this happen to be equal line, you obviously see a butterfly, a flower, a dolphin.","zh":"现在，生物学的研究使人类对周围的世界有了一些深刻的认识。 来看看这四幅全景图吧。 左上角可以看到一些细菌；此外，图中还可以看到蝴蝶、花朵和海豚。（原文 equal line 含义不明，待核对）"},{"en":"If you see that at the outer space, just looks these different forms and structures. You have no idea that they were all related to one to another. So one of the most profound thing that biology told us is that all life on the earth is exceptionally related similar to one to another.","zh":"如果从外部观察，你会发现这些生命形式的形态和结构各不相同。 乍看之下，你可能意识不到它们彼此之间存在联系。 所以生物学告诉我们的最深刻的事情之一就是地球上所有的生命都非常相关且彼此相似。"},{"en":"So, for example, all of these life forms rely on DNA and RNA for storing and transmitting in using their genetic and inherited information. They are all based on cells. Cell is the fundamental building block of all life. All of these organisms consist of cells, and the cells essentially have the same chemicals inside of them - carbon, hydrogen, oxygen and nitrogen, and the whole bunch of other stuff and much smaller amount.","zh":"例如，所有这些生命形式都依赖于DNA和RNA来存储和传输它们的遗传信息。 它们都是基于细胞的。 细胞是所有生命的基本组成部分。 所有这些生物都是由细胞组成的，细胞内部本质上有相同的化学物质——碳、氢、氧、氮，以及其他所有物质，但数量要少得多。"},{"en":"All these organisms conducted metabolism, in other words, chemical reactions that using convert energy from one to the other. And basic chemistry is all very similar to one and another. The type of molecule is used very similar to one and another.","zh":"所有这些生物体都会进行新陈代谢，换句话说，就是通过化学反应将能量从一种形式转化为另一种形式。 它们基本的化学机制也十分相似。 它们所使用的分子类型也十分相似。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S002":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"I'm going to start with Vitamin D today, and I think probably most of you know that Vitamin D is called the \"sunshine vitamin\". And it's called that because there is absolutely no dietary need for Vitamin D if you get adequate sunshine. And I think the really important words here is actually the \"if\" because it turns out that in certain climates which aren't near the equator, there's probably a big question as to whether or not you do get adequate sunshine.","zh":"今天我将从维生素D开始，我想你们大多数人都知道维生素D被称为“阳光维生素”。 之所以这么叫，是因为如果你有充足的阳光，饮食绝对不需要额外补充维生素D。 这里真正重要的是“如果”这个条件，因为在远离赤道的一些地区，人们未必能够获得充足的日照。"},{"en":"So Vitamin D really isn't actually a vitamin. It's a prohormone. When human beings evolve, we evolved in tropical climates and ran around naked with plenty of skin exposure to sunlight, so you know in those time, there was really no dietary need for Vitamin D at all.","zh":"所以维生素D实际上并不是一种维生素。 它是一种激素原。 人类是在热带环境中进化的，当时皮肤大量暴露于阳光之下，因此基本不需要从饮食中额外摄取维生素 D。"},{"en":"But as humans began migrating away from equatorial regions, they actually created a need for Vitamin D in food because the sunlight wasn't adequate, I mean certainly, particularly during the winter months, it was not adequate at all.","zh":"但随着人类开始从赤道地区迁移，因为日照不够充足，他们实际上产生了对食物中维生素D的需求，尤其是在冬季。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S008":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Thirty-one obese women volunteered to participate in a Canadian experiment aimed at testing changes in their body fat. These women were asked to follow strict daily diet requirements and to engage in prescribed exercises every day. The goal was to understand how such a regimen would affect their weight and overall health over time.","zh":"三十一名肥胖女性自愿参加了一项加拿大实验，该实验旨在测试她们体脂的变化。 这些女性被要求遵守严格的每日饮食规定，并每天进行规定的锻炼。 实验的目标是了解这种方案随着时间推移对她们体重和整体健康的影响。"},{"en":"After six months, the results were surprising. Some of the participants lost weight, as expected. However, others showed no change in their weight, and some even gained weight. These unexpected outcomes raised questions about what might have gone wrong, given that all participants were following the same guidelines.","zh":"六个月后，结果令人意外。 如预期所料，有些参与者减轻了体重。 然而，也有些人的体重没有变化，甚至还有人增重了。 这些出乎意料的结果引发了关于可能出错原因的疑问，尽管所有参与者都遵守了相同的指导原则。"},{"en":"There are two possible explanations for these varied results. First, some participants may have cheated on the diet, either intentionally or unintentionally. For example, small deviations in food choices or portion sizes could have impacted their results. Second, psychological factors could have played a role.","zh":"对此，有两种可能的解释。 第一，部分参与者可能在饮食上作弊，无论是有意还是无意的。 例如，食物选择或份量上的小偏差可能影响了结果。 第二，心理因素可能也发挥了作用。"},{"en":"Some participants might have reduced their level of exercise, either consciously or unconsciously. For instance, they may have felt less motivated or justified doing less physical activity because they believed the diet alone would be sufficient. These findings highlight the complexities of weight loss and the importance of understanding not just the physical but also the psychological factors involved in such experiments.","zh":"一些参与者可能降低了运动水平，无论是有意识还是无意识的。 例如，她们可能因为认为仅靠饮食就足够而感到动力不足，或者减少了体力活动的合理性。 这些发现突出了减重的复杂性，以及理解此类实验中不仅是身体因素，还有心理因素的重要性。"},{"en":"They also emphasize the need for ongoing support and monitoring to help individuals stay consistent with their health goals.","zh":"它们还强调了提供持续支持和监督的重要性，以帮助个人保持健康目标的一致性。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S011":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"A: “But what are the dangers of keeping these drugs at home?” B: “There are a number of dangers. Parents should know that leftover drugs are dangerous because they may be accidentally ingested by children. Either adults don’t keep the bottles properly closed and stored or because even many kids can sometimes open childproof lids.","zh":"A:“但是把这些药放在家里有什么危险呢?” B:“有很多危险。 父母应该知道剩余的药物是危险的，因为它们可能会被孩子误服。 要么是成年人没有正确地将瓶子盖好并保存起来，要么就是因为许多孩子有时会打开儿童保护盖。"},{"en":"Patients may use the drugs after their expiration date. The leftover drugs may be taken for the wrong reason. For example, someone may have a viral infection and self-prescribed to left over into microbial that was prescribed for a bacterial infection. But that drug will have no effect as the viral infection.","zh":"患者有可能吃了过期的药。 剩余的药物可能会被胡乱服用。 例如，有人可能感染了病毒，然后自己开了处方，而处方确是针对细菌感染的。"},{"en":"Drugs that are left over might be given to or taken by someone else who may have a serious allergy to the medicine and who for that reason would not be prescribed to medicine under the supervision of a physician. Finally, inappropriate use of drugs promotes drug resistance if the drug is taken for the wrong indication, the wrong duration, or in the wrong dosage. A: “Todd, what can people do about this and how can the situation be improved?”","zh":"剩下的药物可能会给那些对该药有严重过敏反应的人服用，因为他们没有在医生的监督下开处方。 最后，如果用药适应症不正确、用药时间不正确或用药剂量不正确，则会导致耐药。” A:“托德，对此人们能做些什么?"},{"en":"B: “I think physicians, patients and parents of patients can take steps to improve the situation. First of all, physicians should prescribe the drug only when appropriate, only in the correct amount and only for the correct duration. Also, the physician must stress to the patient that the full course of the drug must be taken.","zh":"B:“我认为医生、病人和病人的家长都可以采取措施改善这种情况。 首先，医生要开合适的处方，在合适的时间开合适的剂量。 此外，医生必须向病人强调必须服用整个疗程的药物。"},{"en":"This is recommended even if symptoms resolved before the end of the prescription and parents of children on antibiotics need to ensure they complete their course as well.”","zh":"即使病症在处方结束前消失了，服用药物的孩子的父母也需要确保他们完成整个疗程。”"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S012":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Since the discovery of DNA structure, it was long believed that genes only influence people’s physical structure. This perspective shaped our understanding of genetics for decades, focusing on how genes determine traits like height, eye color, and susceptibility to certain diseases. However, a breakthrough came with the mapping of genes in 2001, which revealed something groundbreaking.","zh":"自从DNA结构的发现以来，人们长期认为基因只会影响人的身体结构。 这种观点塑造了我们对遗传学的理解，持续了数十年，重点关注基因如何决定身高、眼睛颜色以及对某些疾病的易感性等特征。 然而，2001年基因图谱的绘制带来了突破性发现，揭示了令人震惊的新发现。"},{"en":"Researchers found that genes not only affect physical characteristics but also have a genetic responsibility for human psychological behaviors. This discovery fundamentally changed the way we understand our behaviors, emphasizing that our genes play a role in shaping not only our bodies but also our minds. The research on genes has provided integrated and comprehensive information about the intricate relationship between biology and behavior.","zh":"研究人员发现，基因不仅仅影响身体特征，还对人类的心理行为负责。 这一发现从根本上改变了我们对行为的理解，强调了基因在塑造我们身体和大脑方面的作用。 基因研究为我们提供了关于生物学与行为之间复杂关系的整合性和全面性的信息。"},{"en":"These findings have extended beyond genetics, offering valuable insights into fields like biology, psychology, and neuroscience. By connecting genetic data to human behaviors, scientists have opened new pathways for studying mental health, brain function, and even social interactions. This advancement highlights the importance of genetic research in providing a deeper understanding of what makes us who we are.","zh":"这些发现已经超越了遗传学，为生物学、心理学和神经科学等领域提供了宝贵的见解。 通过将基因数据与人类行为联系起来，科学家们为研究心理健康、大脑功能甚至社会互动开辟了新的途径。 这一进展凸显了遗传学研究在更深入理解我们是谁方面的重要性。"},{"en":"It continues to inspire innovations that benefit both science and society, paving the way for more targeted approaches to healthcare and behavioral studies.","zh":"它继续激发着对科学和社会有益的创新，为更有针对性的医疗和行为研究方法铺平了道路。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S014":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Historically, the therapeutic environment has been a subject of significant interest among researchers and healthcare professionals. They discovered that elements such as fresh air and natural daylight play vital roles in enhancing a patient’s recovery process. Beyond these natural elements, the architecture and design of healthcare facilities have been found to exert similarly beneficial effects.","zh":"从历史上看，治疗环境一直是研究人员和医疗专业人士关注的一个重要课题。 他们发现，新鲜空气和自然光等元素在促进患者恢复过程中起着至关重要的作用。 除了这些自然因素，医疗设施的建筑和设计也被发现具有类似的积极作用。"},{"en":"For example, having access to views of hospital gardens or yards can help patients relax, improve their sleep quality, and alleviate both stress and pain more effectively. Interestingly, the connection between a well-designed hospital environment and patient recovery is supported by those who work closest to patients. A survey revealed that 90% of hospital nurses believe that the design and atmosphere of healthcare facilities are directly linked to better recovery outcomes.","zh":"例如，可以看到医院花园或庭院的景色有助于患者放松，改善睡眠质量，更有效地缓解压力和疼痛。 有趣的是，精心设计的医院环境与患者康复之间的联系得到了与患者接触最密切的工作人员的支持。 一项调查显示，90%的医院护士认为，医疗设施的设计和氛围与更好的康复结果直接相关。"},{"en":"This highlights the critical importance of incorporating thoughtful design principles into the creation of healthcare environments, not only for patient well-being but also for enhancing overall treatment effectiveness.","zh":"这突出了在医疗环境的创建中融入周到设计原则的重要性，这不仅有助于患者的身心健康，还能提高整体治疗的效果。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S018":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"We are from an organization called Nonhuman Rights Project, and we fight for legal rights of non-human animals. Drawing a line in order to enslave an autonomous and self-determining being is a violation of equality. We then searched through 80 jurisdictions. We chose the state of New York.","zh":"我们来自一个叫做非人权项目的组织，我们为非人类动物争取合法权利。 为了奴役一个自主的、自我决定的存在而划清界限是对平等的侵犯。 然后我们搜查了80个司法管辖区。 我们选择了纽约州。"},{"en":"Then we decided upon who our plaintiffs are going to be. We decided upon chimpanzees. We know the extraordinary cognitive capabilities that they have, and they also resemble the kind that human beings have. And so we chose chimpanzees, and we began to then canvass the world to find the experts in chimpanzee cognition.","zh":"然后我们决定了原告是谁。 我们决定选择黑猩猩。 我们知道它们拥有非凡的认知能力，它们也类似于人类。 所以我们选择了黑猩猩，然后我们开始在世界范围内寻找黑猩猩认知方面的专家。"},{"en":"So now we needed to find our chimpanzee. Our chimpanzee, first we found two of them in the state of New York. Both of them would die before we could even get our suits filed. Then we found Tommy. Tommy is a chimpanzee. Tommy was a chimpanzee.","zh":"所以现在我们需要找到我们的黑猩猩。 我们的黑猩猩，首先我们在纽约州发现了两只。 我们还没来得及提起诉讼，他们俩就都死了。 然后我们找到了汤米。 汤米是一只黑猩猩。 汤米曾经是一只黑猩猩。"},{"en":"We found him in that cage. We found him in a small room that was filled with cages in a larger warehouse structure on a used trailer lot in central New York. And so on the last week of December 2013, the Nonhuman Rights Project filed three suits all across the state of New York using the same common law argument.","zh":"我们在那个笼子里找到他的。 我们在纽约市中心一个旧拖车停车场的一个更大的仓库里发现了他，房间里满是笼子。 在2013年12月的最后一周，非人权项目在整个纽约州提起了三起诉讼使用了同样的普通法论据。"},{"en":"The court didn't approve our appeal because they think chimpanzees are not humans even though they have cognitive skills. We proved to the court that chimpanzees also have cognitive capabilities, and they were not hearing us. We wanted the chimpanzees out, and we wanted them brought to Save the Chimps, a tremendous chimpanzee sanctuary in South Florida which involves an artificial lake with 12 or 13 islands -- there are two or three acres where two dozen chimpanzees live on each of them.","zh":"法院没有批准我们的上诉，因为他们认为黑猩猩不是人类，尽管它们有认知技能。 我们向法庭证明黑猩猩也有认知能力，但它们没有听我们说话。 我们想要把黑猩猩们放出来，我们想要把他们带到“拯救黑猩猩”项目中 - 这是一个坐落于南弗罗里达的大型黑猩猩保护区，里面有一个人工湖，有12到13个岛屿，有2到3英亩，每个岛屿上住着24只黑猩猩。"},{"en":"And these chimpanzees would then live the life of a chimpanzee, with other chimpanzees in an environment that was as close to Africa as possible.","zh":"然后这些黑猩猩就会过着黑猩猩的生活，和其他黑猩猩一起生活在尽可能接近非洲的环境中。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S020":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"What is the fight or flight response? To understand the fight or flight response, it helps to think about the role of emotions in our lives. Many of us would prefer to focus on our logical thinking nature and ignore our sometimes troublesome emotions. But emotions do have a purpose.","zh":"什么是迎战或逃跑反应? 为了理解“迎战或逃跑”反应，有利于了解情绪在我们生活中的作用会。 我们中的许多人宁愿专注于逻辑思维的本性，而忽略时而令人烦恼的情绪。 但是情绪是有目的的。"},{"en":"Our most basic emotions, like fear, anger or disgust, they are actually vital messengers. They evolved as signals to help us meet our basic needs for self-preservation and safety. It would be dangerous to be indecisive about a threat to our survival. So the brain runs information from our senses through the most primitive, reactive parts of our brains first.","zh":"我们最基本的情绪，比如恐惧、愤怒或厌恶，它们实际上是至关重要的信息传递着。 它们逐步形成信号来帮助我们满足自我保护和安全的基本需求。 在威胁到我们生存的问题上犹豫不决是危险的。 因此，大脑首先通过大脑中最原始、最具反应性的部分来处理来自感官的信息。"},{"en":"These areas of the brain control instinctive responses and they don't do too much thinking. This most primitive part of our brain communicates with the rest of our brain and our body to create signals we can't ignore easily powerful emotions and symptoms. The fight or flight response is a physiological response triggered when we feel a strong emotion such as fear.","zh":"大脑的这些区域控制着最原始的反应，而且不需要任何思索。 我们大脑最原始的部分与我们的大脑和身体的其他部分进行沟通，产生我们不能轻易忽视的信号，强烈的情绪和症状。 “迎战或逃跑反应”是一种生理反应，当我们感受到强烈的情绪，如恐惧时，就会触发这种反应。"},{"en":"Fear is the normal emotion to feel in response to a danger or threat. Fear also has a close relative. We call anxiety. The fight or flight response evolved to enable us to react with appropriate actions, to run away, or to fight, or sometimes to freeze to be a less visible to a target.","zh":"恐惧是面对危险或威胁时的正常情绪。 恐惧也有一个“近亲”。 就是我们所谓的“焦虑”。 迎战或逃跑反应的进化使我们能够做出适当的反应：逃跑，或迎战，或有时什么也不做，让自己不那么明显。"},{"en":"So it's important to think of this as a normal response, but one which can be triggered too often by things which we perceive as a threat to us.","zh":"所以把这看作是一种正常的反应是很重要的，但这种反应往往会被我们认为对我们有威胁的事情触发。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S050":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Worker bees exhibit remarkable altruism, a behavior deeply embedded in their genetic and evolutionary traits. To protect the hive from intruders, worker bees willingly sacrifice their lives, ensuring the safety of the next generation. This selflessness is not just a random occurrence but a critical mechanism for maintaining the colony's survival and stability.","zh":"工蜂展现了非凡的利他行为，这种行为深深植根于其基因和进化特性中。 为了保护蜂巢免受入侵者的威胁，工蜂甘愿牺牲自己的生命，以确保下一代的安全。 这种无私行为并非偶然，而是维持蜂群生存与稳定的关键机制。"},{"en":"Charles Darwin studied this phenomenon and connected it to the broader principles of evolution. He noted that the survival of a bee colony depends heavily on the reproductive success of the queen bee. By enhancing the queen’s ability to produce offspring, the genetic legacy of the entire colony is safeguarded.","zh":"查尔斯·达尔文研究了这一现象，并将其与更广泛的进化原则联系起来。 他指出，蜂群的生存在很大程度上依赖于蜂王的繁殖成功。 通过增强蜂王繁育后代的能力，整个蜂群的基因得以延续。"},{"en":"This intricate system highlights the delicate interplay between individual roles and the collective well-being of the species, shedding light on the evolutionary strategies that have shaped the lives of bees over time.","zh":"这一复杂的系统凸显了个体角色与物种整体福祉之间的微妙平衡，揭示了塑造蜜蜂生活的进化策略。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S115":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Bees use an intricate and fascinating communication system known as the waggle dance. When a bee discovers a rich food source, it returns to the hive and performs a specific dance to communicate the location of the food to the rest of the colony. Through this dance, the bee conveys crucial information, such as the direction, distance, and quality of the food source, by waggling its body and making specific movements.","zh":"蜜蜂使用一种复杂且引人入胜的沟通系统，称为摇摆舞。 当蜜蜂发现丰富的食物来源时，它会返回蜂巢，进行特定的舞蹈，向整个群体传达食物的位置。 通过这舞蹈，蜜蜂传递关键信息，如食物的方向、距离和质量，摇动身体并做出特定的动作。"},{"en":"The speed and angle of the dance indicate how far away the food is, while the direction in which the bee moves relative to the sun indicates the direction. This sophisticated form of communication is not just a random behavior but a well-organized system that allows bees to efficiently share information and cooperate in locating food sources. Moreover, bees also use sounds and vibrations during the dance, further enhancing the message they send to other bees.","zh":"舞蹈的速度和角度表示食物的远近，而蜜蜂相对于太阳移动的方向则指示了食物的方向。 这种复杂的沟通形式不仅仅是一种随机行为，而是一个组织良好的系统，允许蜜蜂高效地分享信息并合作寻找食物来源。 此外，蜜蜂在舞蹈过程中还会使用声音和振动，进一步增强它们传递给其他蜜蜂的信息。"},{"en":"This ability to relay such detailed environmental information shows just how complex and advanced bee behavior can be. It’s a remarkable example of how animals can adapt and communicate in ways that are essential for the survival and functioning of their colony.","zh":"这种传递如此详细的环境信息的能力展示了蜜蜂行为的复杂性和高级性。 它是动物如何适应并通过必要的方式进行沟通的一个非凡例子，这对于其群体的生存和运作至关重要。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S006":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"In my view, it's impossible not to talk about wildlife, and not think about its role in livelihoods. And I guess part of that is my own view, part of the research that I do in Africa. In most east and west Africa. I look at a role, all the humans rely on wildlife as the source of food, and also the source of income.","zh":"在我看来，想要谈论野生动物，不考虑它在生计中的作用是不可能的。 这一部分是我自己的观点，另一部分是我在非洲做的研究。 我发现，所有的人类都依赖野生动物作为食物的来源，也是收入的来源。"},{"en":"And we talk about our wildlife, if we talk about fish, we are talking about what is probably the single most important source of protein for humans across the globe. And so, billions, or more than a billion people rely on fish as their primary source of animal protein, and most of these people live in poverty. So the management of wild fish resources in a sense is incredibly important to livelihoods and health.","zh":"我们谈论野生动物，如果我们谈论鱼类，我们谈论的可能是全球人类唯一的最重要的蛋白质来源。 因此，数十亿人，或者超过十亿人依赖鱼类作为他们动物蛋白质的主要来源，这些人中的大多数生活在贫困中。 所以野生鱼类资源的管理在某种意义上对人们的生计和健康非常重要。"},{"en":"And also, wildlife tourism is the multiple billion dollars’ industry, and in many places, such as Africa and South America, it can be the number one source of income, it can be the number one source of foreign income for economies.","zh":"而且，野生动物旅游是一个价值数十亿美元的产业，在许多地方，比如非洲和南美洲，它可以是第一收入来源，它可以是位列第一的外国经济收入来源。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S007":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"One of the most amazing things that’s happened even in my lifetime is the prediction of cosmology. When I started out forty odd years ago, we thought we knew that the universe began in a Big Bang, although some people doubted that theory even then. We thought the universe was about ten or twenty billion years old.","zh":"在我的有生之年，宇宙学所取得的预测性成果是最令人惊叹的发展之一。 当我四十多年前开始研究宇宙的时候，我们以为我们知道宇宙起源于一次大爆炸，尽管即使在那个时候也有人怀疑这个理论。 我们认为宇宙大约有100到200亿年的历史。"},{"en":"But now for really very sound scientific reasons we can say that the universe started in a Big Bang over 13.8 billion years ago. So it’s not 14, not 13, because of the decimal point in there, and it’s a stunning achievement to know that. And we also know that the laws of physics that apply to tiny particles inside atoms can explain what happened in the Big Bang - you can’t have one without the other.","zh":"但现在，基于非常合理的科学理由我们可以说宇宙起源于138亿年前的大爆炸。 因此，不是简单地说 130 亿或 140 亿年，而是能够精确到 138 亿年；这是一项令人惊叹的科学成就。 我们还知道，支配原子内部微观粒子的物理定律，也能用于解释大爆炸过程中发生的现象；这两个研究领域密不可分。"},{"en":"A very neat example of this is that when you apply nuclear physics, the kind of physics to understand how stars work, you find out that the oldest star in the universe is about 13 billion years old. So their universe is just a little bit older than the stars. Fantastic, if we’ve done it and counted in the other way around and said that the stars were older than the universe, we would say science were in deep trouble.","zh":"一个很好的例子是当你应用核物理，那种理解恒星如何工作的物理，你会发现宇宙中最古老的恒星大约有130亿年的历史。 所以宇宙比恒星的年龄大一点。 太棒了，设想一下，如果我们用另一种方法计算，发现恒星比宇宙更古老，我们就会说科学有大麻烦了。"},{"en":"But it’s not, everything fits together and we know how the universe began, we have come to understand the way it is. We don’t know quite so well what will happen in the future, but we have some ideas, which are as good as those ideas we had 40 years ago about how the Big Bang happened.","zh":"但事实并非如此，现在的数据正好吻合，我们知道了宇宙是如何形成的，我们也了解了宇宙的存在方式。 我们不太清楚未来会发生什么，但我们有一些想法，这些想法和40年前关于大爆炸是如何发生的想法一样好。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S009":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"So various conclusions. Yes, bees are in decline. These declines are well-documented. They are real and supported by good, strong scientific evidence, which is the only evidence counts. The drivers of decline are many, and varied depending on species. The effects of pollinator loss could be absolutely huge.","zh":"下面总结几点结论。 是的，蜜蜂数量在减少。 这些下降是有据可查的。 它们是真实存在的，并且有可靠而有力的科学证据支持，而这才是唯一真正重要的证据。 减少的因素是多种多样的，而且取决于蜜蜂的种类。 传粉者的减少可能产生极其巨大的影响。"},{"en":"So is it a catastrophe? Not yet. But it could be. On the positive side, we are aware of the problem. Awareness is being raised all the time and people are taking actions. Before fixing is missing, you can recognize the problem. At least it's been done.","zh":"那么，这是一场灾难吗? 目前还不算，但将来可能演变成灾难。 从积极的方面来看，我们已经意识到了这个问题。 人们的意识一直在提高，人们也在采取行动。 在缺少修复之前，您可以识别出问题。 至少已经有人这么做了。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S033":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"They're calling it the new GFC, the global food crisis. Prices have doubled in the first decade of this century and are predicted to rise by almost 50 per cent in the next 10 years if the world doesn't change its ways. Thing one, cut the waste. 50 per cent, 30 to 50 per cent of all food that's produced at the moment is thrown out.","zh":"他们称之为新的GFC，全球粮食危机。 在本世纪头10年，粮食价格翻了一番，如果世界不改变其发展方式，预计未来10年将上涨近50%。 第一，减少浪费。"},{"en":"Now, what does that tell us about our production system and our distribution system? That's one of the items for discussion of the Global Food Futures Forum in Brisbane. And it isn't just wealthy white Western nations wasting food. Internationally, waste is a real problem and no more such than in developing countries where the infrastructure is poorly developed, where grain isn't properly dried.","zh":"那么，这对我们的生产系统和分配系统有什么启示呢? 这是在布里斯班举行的全球粮食期货论坛讨论的议题之一。 在国际上，浪费是一个真正的问题，尤其是在基础设施落后、粮食不能正确干燥的发展中国家。"},{"en":"It isn't properly stored in countries in West Africa where I work. We've calculated in some cases 60 per cent of some farmers stocks (that) have been lost due to poor storage and poor processing. Australia is almost completely self-sufficient and feeds another 40 million people overseas.","zh":"在我工作的西非国家，它没有被妥善保存。 澳大利亚几乎完全自给自足，养活了另外4000万海外人口。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S037":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Q:         Why do we need to recycle water? A:         Because we don’t generate much new water. Chemically the process of generating water, which is basically taking hydrogen and oxygen and burning them to produce water, is not a process that happens a lot anymore. So in terms of our total volume of water in the world, yes it is changing, but it’s not changing significantly relative to the rate at which we are using or demand fresh new water.","zh":"问:为什么我们需要循环用水? A:因为我们没有产生太多的新水。 从化学角度来说，生成水的过程，也就是将氢和氧燃烧产生水，已经不是一个经常发生的过程了。 所以就世界上的总水量而言，是的，它在变化，但相对于我们使用或需求新鲜水的速度，它的变化并不显著。"},{"en":"Q: Now there are a lot of different areas of technology involved in water recycling, and we are later in the interview going to get to industrial use and the reclamation of sewerage. What about in the home at the moment; what sort of technology is being utilized in the home when we talk about water recycling?","zh":"Q：现在有很多不同的技术领域涉及到水循环利用，我们在采访中稍后将谈到工业使用和污水回收利用。 此时此刻在家里; 当我们谈到水循环利用时，在家庭中使用了什么样的技术?"},{"en":"A: Well very little on average. Typically in a modern home, we turn on the tap, we take a glass of water, we probably in turning on that tap flush ten glasses of water down the sink. We take a shower, we use fresh water, we do a whole range of things, and there is nominally very little recycling of that.","zh":"A：嗯，平均来说很少。 通常在现代家庭中，我们打开水龙头，拿起一杯水，我们可能在打开水龙头的同时把十杯水冲进水池。 我们洗澡，用新鲜的水，我们做各种各样的事情，而这些水通常很少被循环利用。"},{"en":"It goes down the drain and it goes off to a wastewater treatment plant. There is actually very, very little recycling at a local level. People don’t actually say well I’m now going to take the water I just used, put it through a sophisticated process and reuse it and have a closed loop.","zh":"它进入下水道，然后进入污水处理厂。 实际上，在地方层面上，回收是非常非常少的。 人们不会说我现在要用我刚刚用过的水，把它经过一个复杂的过程，再利用它，形成一个闭环。"},{"en":"It’s not a closed loop in the home.","zh":"这不是家里的一个闭环。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S118":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"There can now be no reasonable, science-based, doubt about the reality of global climate change effects brought on by the cumulative and rapidly growing emission of so-called 'greenhouse' gasses - primarily carbon dioxide - into the atmosphere. As these effects become increasingly more obvious worldwide, so commercial interests, groups of concerned individuals, and national governments have been gripped by what amounts to mass panic about what to do about it. To many, Paul Ehrlich's Malthusian 'Population Bomb' of 1968 appears about to explode in the world's face in an indirect version of his millenarian vision of population growth, which outpaces agricultural production capacity-with predictably catastrophic results for humanity.","zh":"现在对于气候变化影响的事实没有任合合理、基于科学的怀疑，所谓的“温室”气体——主要是二氧化碳——累积并迅速增加排放到大气中，造成了全球气候变化的影响。 随着这些影响在世界范围内变得越来越明显，商业利益集团、相关个人团体和国家政府已经为如何采取大规模措施来应对它所感到恐慌。 在许多人看来，保罗•埃尔利希1968年提出的马尔萨斯式“人口炸弹”似乎即将在世界爆炸，这是他千禧年所设想的人口增长速度超过农业生产能力的景象——可以预见，这将给人类带来灾难性的后果。"},{"en":"And his three-part crisis scenario does indeed seem now to be present: a rapid rate of change, a limit of some sort, and delays in perceiving that limit. Ehrlich's work was roundly criticized at the time, and later, from many quarters, and much of what he predicted did not come about. Nevertheless, can the world afford to take the risk that the climate scientists have got it wrong?","zh":"他提出的危机设想由三部分组成，现在看来确实存在:快速的变化，某种限度，以及对这种限度的延迟认识。 埃利希的研究在当时受到了严厉的批评，后来也受到了来自许多方面的批评，他所预言的很多东西都没有实现。 然而，这个世界能承担得起气候科学家犯错的风险吗？"},{"en":"Is it not in everyone's interests to apply the Precautionary Principle in attempting to avoid the worst of their predictions - now, rather than at some future time? As the Chairman of the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change, Mr. Rajendra Pachauri, has recently pointed out, eleven of the warmest years since instrumental records began have occurred in the past twelve, while major precipitation changes are taking place on a global scale.","zh":"现在运用预防原则来试图避免最坏的预测，而不是在未来的某个时候，难道不符合每个人的利益吗? 政府间气候变化专门委员会(Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change)主席拉金德拉·帕乔里(Rajendra Pachauri)最近指出，自仪器记录开始以来，过去12年有11个最热的年份，而全球范围内发生了重大的降水变化。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S004":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"For thousands of years, philosophers and astronomers and thinkers of all sorts have imagined that the universe, the space around us, was rather like this floor in front of us. It was fixed and unchangeable, and things happen on it, just as people walk around. So the stars, the comets, and the planets, and the other heavenly bodies moved around and traced down their parts on this completely unchanging stage of space.","zh":"数千年来，哲学家、天文学家以及形形色色的思想家们一直设想，我们周围的宇宙空间，其形态大致就像我们眼前的这片地面。 它是固定不变的，事情在其表面发生，就像人在上面走动一样。 因此，恒星、彗星、行星和其他天体都在这个完全不变的空间舞台上运动，并沿着它们各自的部分运动。"},{"en":"In the 20th century, as a result of Einstein’s work, that view of the universe was completely transformed. We began to understand that there was no absolutely fixed stage of space at all on which all celestial notions were played out. But in some sense on the larger scale in the universe, space itself was in this state of a continuous dynamic change.","zh":"在20世纪，由于爱因斯坦的研究，（人们）对宇宙的看法完全改变了。 我们开始认识到，太空中根本不存在绝对固定的阶段，所有天体的概念都在这个阶段上发挥作用。 但从某种意义上说，在宇宙的更大尺度上，空间本身也处于这种持续动态变化的状态。"},{"en":"That was a prediction made by Einstein. But it was the astronomer Edwin Hubble who is the owner of the honor of making the discovery that our universe was really like that.","zh":"这是爱因斯坦的预言。 但是天文学家埃德温·哈勃很荣幸地发现我们的宇宙确实是这样的。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S017":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Automation technology in vehicles has become a hot topic due to its potential to enhance safety, improve fuel efficiency, and reduce human error on the road. According to the American Traffic Safety Regulation, there are different levels of automation, each designed to gradually reduce the need for human intervention. At level four, the vehicle is fully autonomous, meaning it takes complete control of all driving functions.","zh":"汽车自动化技术由于其提升安全性、提高燃油效率并减少道路上人为错误的潜力，已成为热门话题。 根据美国交通安全规定，自动化有不同的等级，每个等级的设计都是为了逐步减少对人工干预的需求。 在四级自动化中，车辆完全自动驾驶，这意味着它完全控制所有驾驶功能。"},{"en":"The driver does not need to engage in any part of the driving process. However, at level three, we enter conditional automation. Here, the vehicle can handle most driving tasks, but the driver must be alert and ready to take control in certain situations, such as emergency scenarios or complex driving conditions.","zh":"驾驶员不需要参与任何驾驶过程的部分。 然而，在三级自动化中，我们进入了条件自动化。 在这里，车辆可以处理大部分驾驶任务，但驾驶员必须保持警觉，并在某些情况下（如紧急情形或复杂的驾驶条件下）准备接管控制。"},{"en":"Level three automation may be the most acceptable option for the public, as it strikes a balance between the convenience of automation and the safety of having the driver available to intervene when needed. This level could offer an effective way to integrate automation into everyday driving, ensuring safety without fully relying on autonomous systems. As the technology continues to develop, it may become a stepping stone towards more advanced levels of vehicle automation in the future.","zh":"三级自动化可能是公众最能接受的选项，因为它在自动化的便利性和驾驶员在需要时可以干预的安全性之间找到了平衡。 这一等级可能为将自动化技术融入日常驾驶提供一种有效的方式，确保安全而不完全依赖自主系统。 随着技术的不断发展，它可能成为未来向更高级别的汽车自动化过渡的跳板。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S027":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"The history of software is of course, very, very new. The whole I.T. industry is is really only 67 years old, which is extraordinary to be so close to the birth of a major new technology, a major new discipline is quite remarkable given where we got to in those 67 years and under progression has been not so much a progression as a stampede because Moore's Law. The rapid expansion in the power of computing and the rapid fall of the cost of computing and storage and communications has made it feasible for information technology to move into all sorts of areas of life that were never originally envisaged.","zh":"当然，软件的历史是非常非常新的。 整个IT行业真的只发展了67年, 这个时间对于一个新技术的诞生,一个主流行业的诞生是非常短暂的。 计算能力的迅速扩张，以及计算、存储和通信成本的迅速下降，使得信息技术进入生活的各方各面成为可能，而这是人们最初从未设想过的。"},{"en":"What has happened is that there has been, as I said, a stampede for people to pick the low hanging fruit. And that is what has guided the development of software and information technology over the past decades and continues to do so with a number of consequences that we will explore.","zh":"正如我所说的，现在的情况是，人们蜂拥着去采摘（IT行业）所带来的成熟果实。 这就是在过去几十年里，软件和信息技术蓬勃发展的原因，也将在未来继续引领人们探索更多的结果。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S030":{"paragraphs":[],"status":"missing_in_firefly","note":"萤火虫原文文档未收录本题；暂不展示 Whisper 转写，以免误导。"},"S052":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"I suppose you wouldn't expect perhaps to find a mathematician in a museum of historical objects. But actually, the objects that I've been drawn to in this museum have quite a lot of mathematical significance. These Neolithic stones discovered in Scotland dating back 5000 years are probably the first examples of humans exploring the concept of symmetry.","zh":"我想你可能不会期望在历史文物博物馆里找到一个数学家。 但实际上，这个博物馆里吸引我的东西有很多数学意义。 这些在苏格兰发现的新石器时代的石头可以追溯到5000年前，可能是人类探索对称概念的第一个例子。"},{"en":"And that's what I do as a practicing mathematician. I spend my life trying to understand what symmetries are possible in nature and in mathematics and abstractly. And here, you know, I've got a connection going back 5000 years to people who are already trying to understand how can I arrange patches on the side of these stone balls in a symmetrical manner?","zh":"这就是我作为一名执业数学家所做的。 我一生都在努力理解在自然界和数学中抽象的对称是可能的。 在这里，你知道，我与5000年前的人们有了联系他们已经在试图理解我如何在这些石球的侧面以对称的方式排列补丁?"},{"en":"One of the intriguing things about these stones is that we don't actually know what they're for. They might have been for divination trying to predict the future. They might have been part of a game. I mean, they look very much like dice, but we don't really think there's any game associated with them.","zh":"这些石头的一个有趣之处在于，我们并不知道它们的用途。 它们可能是用来占卜的试图预测未来。 它们可能是游戏的一部分。 我的意思是，它们看起来很像骰子，但我们并不认为它们与任何游戏有关。"},{"en":"Maybe they were just for chucking around. They're very nice in the hand when you hold them. Well, maybe they were symbols of power in the clan. I suppose that's why I like them, because we don't really know what they are. If I had a theory about why they were doing this, it would be that actually they were starting to be mathematicians,","zh":"也许它们只是用来随便玩玩的。 当你拿着它们的时候，它们的手感非常好。 也许它们是氏族权力的象征。 我想这就是我喜欢它们的原因，因为我们真的不知道它们是什么。 如果我对他们为什么这样做有一个理论，那就是他们实际上开始成为数学家了，"},{"en":"and that here we see the first example of abstract thought at work, that these weren't for a purpose. Mathematics is a great subject, created a lot of the technology around us. But mathematicians... we create mathematical objects for the joy and the beauty. So it would be lovely to think that these didn't actually have a use, that they were just really a celebration of what is possible.","zh":"在这里我们看到了抽象思维在工作中的第一个例子， 这些不是为了某一个目的。 数学是一个伟大的学科，创造了我们周围的很多技术。 但数学家们…我们创造数学对象是为了快乐和美。 所以，如果认为这些实际上没有什么用处，它们只是对可能发生的事情的一种庆祝，那就太好了。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S005":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"What's the literal definition of \"risk\"? Business schools use risk analysis. So, what do you mean by \"risk\", we need a dictionary. When you look at the dictionary, this is literal, the literal definition of risk what it says is, the definition for example, the possibility of injury, a dangerous element or factor, chance of, degree or possibility of such loss, and so on.","zh":"“风险”的字面定义是什么? 商学院使用风险分析。 你说的\"风险\"是什么意思，我们需要一本字典。 当你查字典的时候，这是字面上的，对风险的字面定义它说的是，例如，造成伤害的可能性，一个危险的元素或因素，造成损失的程度或可能性，等等。"},{"en":"So, risk has two parts, if you look at the literal definition of risk one part is the consequence of some kind of particular danger or hazard loss and the other is about the probability of it, chance and consequence, OK? And then at least where the English language is concerned, when you look up the words safe and safety, which you'll learn, it's a little bit of a loop, a little circular argument, that’s free from harm or risks, secure from danger, harm or loss, the condition of being safe and so on for all.","zh":"所以，风险有两部分，如果你看一下风险的字面定义一部分是某种伤害带来的结果或风险损失，另一部分是它的概率，可能性和后果，对吧? 然后至少对于英语而言,当你查找单词“安全和安全性”, 你将了解, 这是一个循环, 循环论证, 意味着不受伤害或风险, 安全远离危险、伤害或损失, 保持安全的条件等等。"},{"en":"And what do we take out of it? At least when we talk about safe at least in the English language, we are talking about something that is safe, or it sounds safe.","zh":"我们能从中学到什么呢? 至少当我们谈论安全的时候，在英语中，我们谈论的是某事是安全的，或者听起来具有安全性。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S010":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Consumers are the core section of any business. In fact, the whole concept of a business is surrounded by the behavior of consumers, and the value for the consumer is a crucial factor. Now, we have to understand a consumer is not to be taken lightly.","zh":"消费者是任何企业的核心部分。 事实上，一个企业的整个概念都是由消费者的行为所包围的，而对消费者的价值是一个至关重要的因素。 现在，我们必须明白，消费者是不能掉以轻心的。"},{"en":"He knows what product he wants. Consumers are extremely smart. They could make decisions about the price and value of products in minutes or sometimes even a few seconds. So a business therefore needs to uplift its brand image. Consumers are willing to pay 15 times more for quality products.","zh":"他知道自己想要什么产品。 消费者非常聪明。 他们可以在几分钟甚至几秒钟内就决定产品的价格和价值。 因此，企业需要提升自己的品牌形象。 消费者愿意为优质产品支付15倍的价格。"},{"en":"However, the conflict starts when manufacturers failed to meet the expectations. This lies in the basic fundamental of engineering in designing a product. Consumers want products like toilet papers to be the softest, but at the same time to be light and strong, something that can be easily torn.","zh":"然而，当制造商未能达到预期时，冲突就开始了。 这是设计产品的工程学的基本原理。 消费者希望像卫生纸这样的产品是最柔软的，但同时又要轻而结实，这样的东西很容易被撕破。"},{"en":"The brand tide is a really good example. There was a problem with shaking the washing powder before being put into the machine as it causes damage to the material of the clothes. Tide had to live up to a lot of expectations from consumers.","zh":"汰渍品牌就是一个很好的例子。 在将洗衣粉放入洗衣机之前，会对衣服的材质造成损伤，这是一个问题。 汰渍必须满足消费者的很多期望。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S013":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Within most developed countries, we have notions of pragmatism, notions of the fact that we have democracies that have succeeded in tempering the market economy. In the 19th century, 18th century industrial revolution had some very negative effects on people, particularly working classes all over the world. We see data where life expectancy was reduced, hikes were reduced.","zh":"在大多数发达国家，我们有实用主义的观念，这是我们拥有民主制成功调解了市场经济的事实。 在19世纪，18世纪的工业革命对人们，特别是全世界的工人阶级，有严重的负面影响。 我们看到的数据显示，预期寿命降低了，增长率降低了。"},{"en":"We can look at medical records and see that actually living standards in much of the large fractions of the population actually went down. But eventually we passed legislation about working conditions and eventually we circumscribed some of the worst kinds of behavior. We eventually in the 20th century, we put in regulations that impose better environmental conditions.","zh":"我们可以从医疗记录中看到大部分人的生活水平都下降了。 但最终我们通过了有关工作条件的立法，限制了一些最恶劣的行为。 最终在20世纪，我们制定了规章制度来改善环境条件。"},{"en":"And so some of the damage was reversed. And we have made the market economy work in ways that the benefits of it are at least far more widely shared than they were 100 years ago.","zh":"所以逆转了一些损害。 我们已经使市场经济发挥作用，它的益处至少比100年前更广泛分享。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S016":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"The economic models of newspapers are undergoing a dramatic collapse. Over the last half of the 20th century, the newspaper industry has been shrinking significantly. One major reason for this decline is the decreasing number of advertisers and readers, which has drastically affected the financial stability of many newspaper publishers.","zh":"报纸的经济模式正经历剧烈的崩溃。 在20世纪下半叶，报纸行业已经显著缩小。 导致这一衰退的一个主要原因是广告商和读者的数量减少，这严重影响了许多报纸出版商的财务稳定。"},{"en":"Some publishers find themselves struggling to maintain cash flow, either operating in the red or barely breaking even. As a result, numerous newspapers have reduced their publication frequency, moving from daily prints to fewer editions. Others have transitioned entirely to online platforms in an attempt to adapt to changing consumer habits.","zh":"一些出版商发现自己在维持现金流方面苦苦挣扎，要么处于亏损状态，要么勉强盈亏平衡。 因此，许多报纸减少了出版频率，从每日出版减少到更少的版本。 其他报纸则完全转向在线平台，以适应消费者习惯的变化。"},{"en":"This shift has also had a profound impact on employment in the industry. Over the years, the number of staff working in the newspaper sector has plummeted by 30% to 40%. These changes highlight the challenges faced by traditional newspapers in the modern era, forcing the industry to rethink its strategies for sustainability and relevance in the digital age.","zh":"这种转变还对行业的就业产生了深远的影响。 多年来，报纸行业的员工人数已下降了30%到40%。 这些变化突显了传统报纸在现代时代面临的挑战，迫使行业重新思考其在数字时代的可持续性和相关性战略。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S025":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Although managers often have busy schedules, it is important for them to dedicate time to read books, attend seminars, and continue their education in order to improve their leadership and decision-making skills. The most effective managers are not necessarily those who have a deep, intuitive understanding of their specific organization, but rather those who possess a solid grounding in management principles and a broad perspective on business. In fact, a manager who is well-versed in management theories, organizational behavior, and leadership strategies is likely to navigate challenges with more efficiency and insight.","zh":"尽管管理者通常有繁忙的日程安排，但他们仍然需要抽出时间阅读书籍、参加研讨会并持续教育自己，以提高领导力和决策能力。 最有效的管理者不一定是那些对其特定组织有深入直觉理解的人，而是那些拥有扎实管理原理基础和广泛商业视野的人。 事实上，一位精通管理理论、组织行为和领导策略的管理者往往能够更高效且有洞察力地应对挑战。"},{"en":"Experience in the field is certainly valuable, but it should not be the sole factor in determining a manager's effectiveness. In today’s fast-paced and ever-changing business environment, knowledge of current management trends and tools can make all the difference. A manager who is committed to lifelong learning, through formal education or self-study, will be better equipped to make informed decisions, inspire their team, and drive the organization toward long-term success.","zh":"行业经验无疑是宝贵的，但它不应是评判管理者有效性的唯一标准。 在今天这个快速变化的商业环境中，了解当前的管理趋势和工具至关重要。 一位致力于终身学习的管理者，无论是通过正式教育还是自学，都能更好地做出明智决策，激励团队，并推动组织实现长期成功。"},{"en":"Moreover, investing in management knowledge provides a solid foundation for fostering innovation, improving communication, and leading with confidence. Managers who understand key concepts such as strategic planning, conflict resolution, and organizational development are more likely to inspire trust and respect within their teams. Therefore, learning management is not just a career-enhancing skill—it is an essential part of being an effective leader who can guide their organization through complex challenges and growth opportunities.","zh":"此外，投资于管理知识为培养创新、改善沟通和自信领导提供了坚实的基础。 理解战略规划、冲突解决和组织发展等关键概念的管理者更有可能在团队中激发信任和尊重。 因此，学习管理不仅是提升职业发展的技能——它是成为一名有效领导者的必备素质，能够引导组织应对复杂挑战和发展机遇。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S026":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"An experiment on customer behavior explored the impact of messaging strategies on the usage of inactive credit cards. Participants were divided into two groups, each receiving a different type of communication. One group was presented with messages highlighting the benefits they could gain from using their credit cards, such as rewards or cash-back incentives.","zh":"一项关于顾客行为的实验探讨了信息传递策略对非活跃信用卡使用的影响。 参与者被分为两组，每组收到不同类型的沟通信息。 一组接收到的信息强调了使用信用卡可以获得的好处，例如奖励或现金返还激励。"},{"en":"The other group received messages emphasizing potential penalties or missed opportunities if they failed to use their cards, such as losing loyalty points or account privileges. The findings revealed a significant psychological difference in customer motivation based on the type of message. Customers who were informed about potential losses exhibited a stronger inclination to activate and use their cards compared to those who were promised gains.","zh":"另一组接收到的信息则侧重于如果不使用信用卡可能面临的惩罚或错失的机会，例如失去忠诚积分或账户特权。 研究结果显示，根据信息类型，顾客的动机存在显著的心理差异。 接收到潜在损失信息的顾客相比接收到潜在收益信息的顾客，更倾向于激活并使用信用卡。"},{"en":"This outcome aligns with the well-established concept in behavioral economics known as \"loss aversion,\" which suggests that individuals tend to prioritize avoiding losses over acquiring equivalent gains. These results have practical implications for marketing strategies and customer engagement. Businesses might achieve better outcomes by framing their offers in terms of what customers stand to lose rather than solely focusing on potential benefits.","zh":"这一结果与行为经济学中广为人知的“损失厌恶”概念一致，该理论表明人们更倾向于优先避免损失而非获取等量收益。 这些结果对市场营销策略和客户参与度具有实际意义。 企业通过以顾客可能失去的内容来框架其优惠，而不仅仅专注于潜在利益，可能会取得更好的效果。"},{"en":"This approach taps into a deeper emotional response, prompting action and increasing customer participation. Such insights underscore the importance of understanding human psychology in shaping consumer behavior and crafting effective communication strategies.","zh":"这种方法触发了更深层次的情感反应，从而促进行动并提高客户参与度。 这些见解强调了理解人类心理在塑造消费者行为和制定有效沟通策略中的重要性。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S034":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"One essential feature of a successful entrepreneur is to have great ideas, but the definition of a great idea can vary depending on whom you ask. Different people may judge an idea from different perspectives, so there is not always a single fixed standard. A great idea should have several important characteristics.","zh":"成功企业家的一个重要特征是拥有出色的想法，但“好想法”的定义会因人而异。 不同的人可能会从不同角度来评判一个想法，因此并不存在唯一固定的标准。 一个优秀的想法应当具备几个重要特征。"},{"en":"These characteristics help people decide whether an idea has real value and whether it can become the basis of a successful business. It does not necessarily need to be novel, as in completely new. In other words, a great idea does not always have to be something that has never existed before.","zh":"这些特征能够帮助人们判断一个想法是否真正有价值，以及它是否能够成为成功企业的基础。 它不一定必须是全新的，也就是说，并不一定非得是以前从未存在过的东西。 换句话说，一个好想法并不总是意味着完全前所未有。"},{"en":"But it should be unique, something that no one has thought of in exactly the same way before. This means the idea should have its own distinctive feature or approach. And also, a good idea must be protectable. This is somewhat linked to intellectual property, which we will come back and talk about later.","zh":"但它应该具有独特性，也就是别人从未以完全相同的方式想到过。 这意味着这个想法应当拥有自己鲜明的特点或方法。 此外，一个好想法还必须是可以被保护的。 这在某种程度上与知识产权有关，之后我们还会进一步讨论这一点。"},{"en":"If an idea can be protected, it is more likely to give the entrepreneur a clear advantage. It also means that other people cannot simply copy it immediately. And a truly great idea should also be transformative. It can influence the way people do things, solve existing problems, or create a different situation from the one that existed before.","zh":"如果一个想法能够受到保护，那么它更有可能为企业家带来明确的优势。 同时，这也意味着其他人无法立刻简单地复制它。 而一个真正伟大的想法还应当具有变革性。 它能够影响人们做事的方式、解决现有问题，或者创造出一种不同于过去的新局面。"},{"en":"This is to say that it can change the status quo.","zh":"也就是说，它能够改变现状。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S043":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"The stock market is where investors connect to buy and sell investments — most commonly, stocks, which are shares of ownership in a public company. When you need groceries, you go to the supermarket. When you're ready to buy stocks or mutual funds, you'll usually buy them online through the stock market, which anyone can access with a brokerage account or employee retirement plan.","zh":"当你需要购买杂货时，你会去超市。 当你准备购买股票或共同基金时，通常会通过股票市场在线购买，任何人都可以通过经纪账户或雇员退休计划进入股票市场。 \"股票市场\"一词通常指的是主要的股票市场指数之一。"},{"en":"The term 'stock market' often refers to one of the major stock market indexes. However, there are some different uses of the stock market before and after. In the 18th century, manufacturing companies came into the market. Traditional companies used stocks to raise money, and input money into companies, while modern companies used stocks to output money.","zh":"然而，股票市场在历史上有着不同的用途。 在18世纪，制造公司进入了市场。 传统公司利用股票筹集资金，将资金注入公司，而现代公司则通过股票输出资金。 然而，从19世纪到20世纪，像苹果、谷歌和微软这样的现代公司足够强大，可以自己赚钱，并且以不同的方式使用股票。"},{"en":"From 19th to 20th century, however, modern companies, such as Apple, Google and Microsoft are big enough to earn money, and use stocks differently.","zh":"股票市场也倾向于将资金投入大公司。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S044":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"The question today of what makes a luxury brand and how do we distinguish it is very hard to answer. The standard business response is to say they are more exclusive. And we get this exclusivity by having high prices and relatively small amounts of the product available.","zh":"如今是什么造就了一个奢侈品牌，我们如何区分它，这个问题很难回答。 标准的商业回应是说他们更具有排他性。 我们通过高价格和相对少量的产品获得了这种排他性。"},{"en":"The reality, however, of luxury brands is that they are sold in their millions, and in some cases, are not priced that much higher than the standard output. So the only way I can really answer your question is to say it is all relative. As you said in your introduction, it wasn't that long ago in Australia that we would have considered two televisions to be a luxury, or even further back, one color television.","zh":"然而奢侈品牌的现实情况是，它们的销量高达数百万，而且在某些情况下，它们的定价并不比标准产品高出太多。 所以我能真正回答你问题的唯一方法就是说这都是相对的。 就像你在介绍中说的那样，不久以前在澳大利亚我们还认为两台电视机是奢侈品，甚至在更早的时候，一台彩色电视机也是奢侈品。"},{"en":"And you can make a strong argument, for example, that Starbucks in China, right now, is a luxury purchase because of its cost, because of how frequently it is purchased by many people. So, I think the long answer is a complicated one, but the answer is – it depends on whom you talk to. I think in the business community, what we would say is that there is a small cluster of more expensive brands which have a distinct strategy that we would identify as being luxury brands.","zh":"你可以提出一个强有力的论点，例如，星巴克现在在中国是一种奢侈品，因为它的价格，因为它被很多人经常购买。 所以，我认为长篇大论的答案是一个复杂的问题，但答案是——这取决于你和谁交谈。 我认为，在商界我们会说的是，有一小群更昂贵的品牌，它们有一个独特的战略，我们将其定义为奢侈品牌。"},{"en":"And they start with the Rolls Royce and the Tiffanys and the Louis Vuittons of the world. And, l think that tends to be how we see them.","zh":"他们从劳斯莱斯、蒂凡尼和路易威登开始。 我想这就是我们对他们的看法。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S051":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"The advancement of machines serves as a critical indicator of a nation’s development and progress. Today, machines have become incredibly sophisticated, with technologies like face recognition and natural language processing transforming how we live and work. Our dependence on machines has grown significantly, not only improving daily life but also providing avenues for economic gain and innovation.","zh":"机器的进步是衡量一个国家发展与进步的重要指标。 如今，机器已经变得极为先进，诸如面部识别和自然语言处理等技术正在改变我们的生活和工作方式。 我们对机器的依赖显著增加，不仅改善了日常生活，也为经济收益和创新提供了途径。"},{"en":"However, this growing reliance on automation brings challenges, particularly in employment. The increase in the use of machines often leads to job losses or large-scale redundancies. For example, bus drivers are among the occupations most likely to be replaced by automation, and many may need to transition into retail or other service-sector roles. To balance these advancements and address rising unemployment rates, it is essential to develop new industries and opportunities that can absorb the workforce affected by automation.","zh":"然而，这种对自动化日益增长的依赖也带来了挑战，尤其是在就业方面。 机器使用的增加往往导致岗位流失或者出现大面积的裁员。 为平衡这些进步并解决不断上升的失业率问题，有必要发展新的行业和机会，以吸纳因自动化而受影响的劳动力。"},{"en":"Without proactive measures, we will surely see more and more people losing their jobs, with the unemployment rate increasing.","zh":"如果没有积极的措施，我们一定会看到越来越多的人失去工作，失业率一路飙升。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S117":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Today, a university like the LSE in London certainly has to acknowledge that it isn't competition for the best students, all of whom have choices they can exercise - and many of them - choices which run across national and continental borders. So, we are really in a competition, too for staff. The academic job market is one of the most global 25 there is.","zh":"如今，像伦敦政治经济学院这样的大学必须认识到，自己正处于争夺优秀学生的竞争中。这些学生拥有自主选择权，而且许多人的选择跨越国界和洲界。（英文原文的否定结构存疑） 所以，我们真正要争夺的，还有员工。 学术人才就业市场是全球化程度最高的就业市场之一。（原文“25”含义不明，待核对）"},{"en":"And in the 21st century, English is like the new Latin. So universities in English speaking countries are really exposed to more intense competition than those elsewhere. We are in competition for government funding through the assessment of research quality. We are also in competition for research contracts from public and private sector sources.","zh":"在21世纪，英语就像新的拉丁语。 所以说英语国家的大学比其他国家的大学面临着更激烈的竞争。 我们通过评估研究质量来竞争政府资助。 我们还在竞争来自公共和私营部门的研究合同。"},{"en":"And indeed, we are also in competition for the philanthropy pound. So, many of our own donors were at more than one university and indeed, think of the LSE requests alongside those of other charities to which they are committed. That is a competition environment which is particularly visible to someone, like a vice-chancellor.","zh":"事实上，我们也在争夺慈善款项。 因此，我们的许多捐赠者会在不止一所大学（进行捐赠）；确实，想想伦敦政治经济学院的请求，以及捐赠者们所承诺的对其他慈善机构的请求（你就能明白了）。 这是一个竞争环境，对于像英国的大学校长这样的人来说尤其明显。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S003":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Globalization, what is globalization? I think that is takes on a few different definitions. In one sense of the word, globalization means proliferation of transactions across a country. So, one way of thinking about globalization is that it is a way to describe a country's increase in international communications, more trade between countries, and being less self-sufficient in providing goods to their people, and having more companies that have offices in multiple countries, which we call multinationals.","zh":"全球化，什么是全球化? 我认为它有几种不同的定义。 从这个词的某种意义上说，全球化意味着跨越国家的贸易扩散。 因此，思考全球化的其中一种方式是：它作为一种方法来描述一个国家国际交流的增多、国际贸易增长、自给自足提供商品给国民的情况减少、并且有更多的公司在多个国家设有办事处（我们称之为“跨国公司”）。"},{"en":"In other words, it is the source of growth in travel, communication, and corporate trade across borders. And this way of thinking about globalization is the continuation of thinking that has been around for a long time, such as when the Europeans went to the Orient to find spices, which was also an example of global trade and communication. Another way to think of globalization though, is as an economic system.","zh":"换句话说，它是旅游、交流和跨国公司贸易增长的来源。 这种思考全球化的方式是长期存在的思考的延续，比如当欧洲人去东方寻找香料时，这也是全球贸易和交流的一个例子。 另一种看待全球化的方式是，把它看作一个经济体系。"},{"en":"It is a system in which countries became integrated in a way that had never been seen before. In this system, we see a global split in the process between consuming and producing goods. Some countries produce goods, some countries consume goods; and then these countries, in different areas of the globe, depend on each other in a kind of organic solidarity, rather than having an economic system being just inside your country.","zh":"在这个体系中，各国以前所未有的方式融合在一起。 在这个体系中，我们看到了消费和生产过程中的全球分裂。 有的国家生产商品，有的国家消费商品; 然后这些国家，在全球不同的地区，以一种有机团结的方式相互依赖，而不是仅仅在你的国家内部建立一个经济体系。"},{"en":"This system is the way the economy in your country depends on the economy of another country. And in fact, this way of thinking about globalization represents a new era of economic progression. The post-industrial economy has been a global issue.","zh":"这种制度是一国经济依赖另一国经济的方式。 事实上，这种思考全球化的方式代表了一个经济发展的新时代。 后工业经济已经成为一个全球性的问题。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S019":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"The separation of powers is a fundamental principle that underpins the structure of government in many democratic systems, particularly in the United States. The Constitution outlines three distinct branches of government: the legislative branch, which is responsible for making laws; the executive branch, headed by the president, who enforces and implements these laws; and the judicial branch, which interprets the laws. This division of responsibilities ensures that no one branch has too much power, and it provides a system of checks and balances.","zh":"权力分立是许多民主制度中政府结构的基本原则，特别是在美国。 宪法规定了三种独立的政府部门：立法部门，负责制定法律；行政部门，由总统领导，负责执行和实施这些法律；以及司法部门，负责解释法律。 这种职能分工确保没有任何一个部门拥有过多的权力，并提供了一个制衡系统。"},{"en":"However, in the last century, the lines between the legislative and executive branches have become increasingly blurred. While the legislative branch, Congress, is still the primary body responsible for creating laws, the president has gained more influence in the legislative process. This shift has been driven by factors such as the growing role of the executive in setting national agendas, the rise of executive orders, and the expansion of the federal bureaucracy.","zh":"然而，在过去的一个世纪里，立法部门和行政部门之间的界限变得越来越模糊。 虽然立法部门——国会——仍然是主要的法律制定机构，但总统在立法过程中获得了更多的影响力。 这种变化是由多个因素推动的，如行政部门在制定国家议程中的作用日益增加、行政命令的兴起以及联邦官僚机构的扩张。"},{"en":"As a result, the balance of power has shifted, leading to a closer relationship between the executive and legislative branches. This change has sparked debates about the proper role of each branch and whether the system of checks and balances is still functioning as intended.","zh":"因此，权力的平衡发生了变化，行政部门和立法部门之间的关系更加紧密。 这一变化引发了关于各部门应承担的适当角色以及制衡系统是否仍然按预期运作的辩论"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S022":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"So, I think you all know what I mean by globalization, don't you? This is the idea that we all live in a global village. With instant communications, we can share ideas, and consume cultural artifacts from countries all over the world, just by going into the Internet and all dream up, basically.","zh":"我想你们都知道我说的全球化是什么意思，对吧? 这就是我们都生活在一个地球村的想法。 有了即时通信，我们可以分享想法，消费来自世界各国的文化产品，只需进入互联网，基本上所有的梦想。"},{"en":"The world is shrinking. In terms of speeds, it is accelerating, but in terms of distance, it's shrinking. What do I mean by detraditionalization? I mean the disappearance or the erosion, for the better word to use, the erosion of traditional cultures, of conventional ways of doing things, of conventional moralities.","zh":"世界正在缩小。 就速度而言，它在加速，但就距离而言，它在缩小。 我说的去传统化是什么意思? 我指的是消失或侵蚀，用一个更好的词来形容，传统文化的侵蚀，传统做事方式的侵蚀，传统道德的侵蚀。"},{"en":"More and more young people around the world are rejecting the culture they grow up in, and it's probably a little bit cruel. But some imitating a Hollywood model of society, rather than the one which they inherit from their local tradition background.","zh":"世界上越来越多的年轻人正在拒绝他们成长的文化，这可能有点残忍。 但有些人模仿的是好莱坞的社会模式，而不是他们从当地传统背景继承的社会模式。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S024":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Australia, being a multicultural country, is home to immigrants from all over the world, which has contributed to making it a place where some of the world’s oldest continuous cultures thrive. This blend of various cultures is a defining characteristic of Australian society, offering a unique fusion of traditions, languages, and customs. Cultural diversity in Australia provides numerous benefits, especially in areas such as productivity, economic performance, and the labor force.","zh":"澳大利亚作为一个多元文化的国家，是来自世界各地移民的家园，这使得它成为了世界上最古老的连续文化之一的繁荣之地。 这种各种文化的融合是澳大利亚社会的一个鲜明特点，提供了传统、语言和习俗的独特融合。 澳大利亚的文化多样性带来了许多好处，特别是在生产力、经济表现和劳动力等领域。"},{"en":"Immigrants bring with them a wide range of skills, experiences, and worldviews, which enrich the country’s social fabric and economic landscape. Their contributions help drive innovation, increase adaptability, and improve global competitiveness, which are all vital for Australia's success in an interconnected world. Furthermore, cultural diversity fosters creativity by encouraging new ideas and solutions to problems.","zh":"移民带来了广泛的技能、经验和世界观，这些都丰富了国家的社会结构和经济格局。 他们的贡献推动了创新、增强了适应能力，并提高了全球竞争力，这些都是澳大利亚在互联互通的世界中成功所必需的。 此外，文化多样性通过鼓励新想法和解决问题的方案促进了创造力。"},{"en":"It also promotes inclusivity and understanding, as people from various backgrounds learn to work together and appreciate each other’s perspectives. This diverse workforce, in turn, leads to higher levels of productivity and growth. According to recent statistics, nearly half of Australia’s population was either born overseas or has at least one foreign-born parent, further underscoring the significant role immigration has played in shaping the nation.","zh":"它还促进了包容性和理解，因为来自不同背景的人们学会一起工作并欣赏彼此的观点。 这种多元化的劳动力反过来促进了更高水平的生产力和增长。 根据最近的统计数据，澳大利亚近一半的人口要么出生在海外，要么至少有一个外籍父母，这进一步强调了移民在塑造国家中的重要作用。"},{"en":"As a result, the cultural mix in Australia not only enriches the nation socially but also brings a variety of economic benefits, making Australia a more resilient, creative, and globally competitive nation.","zh":"因此，澳大利亚的文化混合不仅丰富了国家的社会面貌，还带来了各种经济利益，使澳大利亚成为一个更加韧性强、富有创意和全球竞争力的国家。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S028":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"One of the things that was going on during the Great Depression was the beginning of the sort of modern food technology that rules, you know, the way American eat Americans eat today. That is, there are a lot of canned foods where banks are coming onto the market at the time. And also, refrigerators were really becoming very, very popular during the Great Depression, both in cities and in rural parts of the country.","zh":"大萧条期间发生的一件事是现代食品技术的开始，你知道，现代食品技术决定了美国人今天的饮食方式。 也就是说，当时有很多罐头食品银行正在进入市场。 而且，冰箱在大萧条时期非常非常流行，在城市和农村地区都是如此。"},{"en":"Thanks to electrification, the Rural Electrification Administration, people could buy appliances, you know, farmers could buy appliances, and that meant frozen foods were becoming big. And, you know, at that time few people could afford to buy them during the early years of the Great Depression. But, you know, gradually these things picked up.","zh":"多亏了电气化，农村电气化管理局，人们可以买电器，你知道，农民可以买电器，这意味着冷冻食品变得越来越大。 你知道，在大萧条的早期，当时很少有人买得起。 但是，你知道，慢慢地，这些事情就会发生。"},{"en":"And so this was like the beginning of the era when people were starting to think about supermarkets with rows and rows of freezer cases and rows and rows of canned foods.","zh":"这就像是那个时代的开始人们开始考虑超市里有一排排的冷冻柜和一排排的罐头食品。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S029":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"But you can see from the relatively crooked and narrow streets of the city of Rome as they look from above today. You can see that again, the city grew in a fairly ad hoc way, as I mentioned. It wasn't planned all at once.","zh":"但你可以从今天罗马城相对弯曲和狭窄的街道上看到它们。 你可以再次看到，这个城市以一种特别的方式发展，就像我提到的那样。 这不是一下子就计划好的。"},{"en":"It just grew up over time, beginning in the eighth century B.C. Now this is interesting because what we know about the Romans is when they were left to own devices and they could build the city from scratch, they didn’t let it grow in an ad hoc way. They structure it in a, in a very careful, in a very methodical way.","zh":"它是随着时间的推移而发展起来的，从公元前八世纪开始。 这很有趣，因为我们对罗马人的了解是如果让他们自己来建造，他们完全可以从零开始建造城市，他们不会让城市以一种特殊的方式发展。 他们以一种非常谨慎，非常有条理的方式来组织它。"},{"en":"That was basically based on military strategy, military planning. The Romans they couldn't have conquered the world without obviously having a masterful military enterprise and everywhere they went on their various campaigns, their various military campaigns. They would build, build camps and those camps were always laid out in a very geometric plan along a grid, usually square or rectangular.","zh":"那基本上是基于军事战略，军事规划。 罗马人如果没有强大的军事力量是不可能征服世界,罗马人四处征战。 他们会建造，建造营地，这些营地总是沿着一个网格，通常是正方形或长方形的几何布局。"},{"en":"So, when we begin to see the Romans building their ideal Roman city, they turn to that so call Castrum or military camp design.","zh":"所以，当我们开始看到罗马人建造他们理想的罗马城市时，他们转向了所谓的Castrum或军营设计。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S035":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"The design of buildings is important according to architectural textbooks. At its roots, architecture exists to create the physical environment in which people live, but architecture is more than just the built environment, it’s also a part of our culture. It stands as a representation of how we see ourselves, as well as how we see the world.","zh":"根据建筑教科书，建筑的设计是很重要的。 从根本上说，建筑的存在是为了创造人们生活的物理环境，但建筑不仅仅是建筑环境，它也是我们文化的一部分。 它代表着我们如何看待自己，以及我们如何看待世界。"},{"en":"There are poorly designed buildings, but also some great building works. In the Victorian Era, architects designed buildings based on bricks and other materials. The design of flaws was based on lighting as it would not only affect appearance but also health conditions. The materials that buildings are made of also matter.","zh":"有设计糟糕的建筑，但也有一些伟大的建筑作品。 在维多利亚时代，建筑师以砖和其他材料为基础设计建筑. 缺陷的设计是基于照明，因为它不仅会影响外观，而且会影响健康状况。 建造建筑的材料也是物质。"},{"en":"For example, the design of the ground floors must ensure that the building is able to withstand the weight of the higher levels. In the 20th century, many old buildings with design flaws were demolished or modified through a natural selection process, which means they are in an altered state rather than an original state. This is an application of Darwin's theory of natural selection to modification of old buildings, which means buildings should adapt to the new world to survive or be pulled down.","zh":"例如，地面层的设计必须确保建筑能够承受更高楼层的重量。 在20世纪，许多设计缺陷的老建筑通过自然选择的过程被拆除或改造，这意味着它们是一种被改变的状态，而不是原始状态。 这是达尔文的自然选择理论在改造旧建筑上的应用，这意味着建筑应该适应新的世界来生存，或者被推倒。"},{"en":"So, it's argued to be unfair to criticize the demolition, although some people believe that whether to be remained should be decided based on their nature and functions. As the world became more and more connected, the styles evolved, but even in modern construction, there is still an importance in honoring the cultural nuances in the built environment.","zh":"因此，有人认为批评拆迁是不公平的，尽管有些人认为是否保留应该根据他们的性质和功能来决定。 随着世界的联系越来越紧密，建筑风格也在演变，但即使是在现代建筑中，尊重建筑环境中的文化差异仍然很重要。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S038":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Globalization is an overused and often misunderstood concept. We hear it all the time on news broadcasts and in any type of public discussion. But the starting point for understanding globalization is that it is industries and markets that globalize, not countries. That’s why it’s helpful to think of Globalization as ‘the integration of economic activities across borders’.","zh":"全球化是一个被滥用和经常被误解的概念。 我们一直在新闻广播和任何类型的公共讨论中听到它。 但理解全球化的出发点是，全球化的是产业和市场，而不是国家。 这就是为什么认为全球化是“跨国界经济活动的一体化”是有益的。"},{"en":"But why does globalization matter? would argue globalization matters because it means the rise of interconnectedness between countries and markets across the world. For example, one of the reasons why the financial crash of 2007/2008 was so serious was because the financial and banking systems of countries around the world have become so closely interconnected with the globalization of markets.","zh":"但为什么全球化如此重要? 我认为全球化很重要，因为它意味着世界各国和市场之间相互联系的增强。 例如，2007/2008年金融危机如此严重的原因之一是，世界各国的金融和银行体系与市场的全球化联系得如此紧密。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S039":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"We have done a social science research on capacity of families and found this compelling and disturbing fact. The most disturbing thing to me is that well-educated parents can always promise their children a prosperous future because these children have sufficient educational capacity and support since they were born. The life chance of a child was set when they were five years old.","zh":"我们对家庭的能力进行了社会科学研究，发现了这一令人信服和不安的事实。 最让我不安的是，受过良好教育的父母总是能承诺他们的孩子一个繁荣的未来，因为这些孩子从出生起就有足够的教育能力和支持。 一个孩子的生存机会在他五岁时就决定了。"},{"en":"Well, this finding has been quite disturbing to me. And, I have to confess that currently there is no obvious way to address this deep root of inequality in our society.","zh":"这个发现让我很不安。 而且，我必须承认，目前，没有明显的方法来解决我们社会中这种根深蒂固的不平等。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S100":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Why should we read the Republic? I image lots of students asked this question to me when they’re given it as a set book at the beginning of their university course, but in fact there are many good reasons to read the Republic. And first one I would pick on is just that it is immensely readable.","zh":"我们为什么要读《理想国》? 我想很多学生在大学课程开始的时候就问过我这个问题，但事实上有很多很好的理由去读《理想国》。 首先，我想说的是，它非常易读。"},{"en":"It’s not Plato did not write philosophy like a dry text book. He wrote it like a living conversation. The whole of the Republic which is fairly fat book is a living conversation written in short almost soundbite type answers, but nevertheless, developing some very important ideas so my first answer then we should read the Republic just because it is readable.","zh":"并不是柏拉图没有把哲学写成一本干巴巴的书。 他把它写得像一场活生生的对话。 《理想国》是一本很厚的书，它是一段活生生的对话，用很短的片段式的回答写成，但还是发展了一些非常重要的想法，所以我的第一个答案是我们应该读《理想国》因为它是可读的。"},{"en":"It is readable. It was written by a genius and it’s worth reading. It’s easy to read. It’s not difficult. But then there’s also obviously the thoughts, the content of the book and he’s asking this absolutely fundamental question why should we bother to be good, what’s in it for us effectively.","zh":"它是可读的。 这是一个天才写的，值得一读。 很容易读懂。 这不是困难的。 但显然还有书的思想和内容，他问的是一个非常基本的问题，为什么我们要费神去做好事，它对我们有什么有效的好处。"},{"en":"It seems when we look at the world, it looks as though injustice pays. It looks as though crime pays or as the good people get trodden down. So, Plato addresses this absolutely fundamental question why should we be good. I’m not going to tell you his answer. Read the book.","zh":"当我们看世界的时候，似乎不公正会带来回报。 看来犯罪是有好处的或者好人被践踏。 柏拉图解决了这个最基本的问题为什么我们应该是善的。 我不会告诉你他的答案。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S040":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Through the 1950s and into the 1960s, the idea of the Industrial Revolution was that it was the work of some genius inventors who created machines used primarily in the textile industry — but also in mining — that eliminated blocks to assembly line production. Then everybody was crowded into factories and the new brave world opened up. In fact, one of the most interesting books and great classics that is still in print was written by an economic historian at Harvard who’s still around called David Landes.","zh":"从20世纪50年代到60年代，工业革命的理念是，一些天才发明家创造了主要用于纺织工业的机器，但也用于采矿，从而消除了装配线生产的积木。 然后大家都挤进了工厂，并且新的美丽世界开始了. 事实上，至今仍在印刷的最有趣的书和最伟大的经典之一是哈佛经济历史学家大卫·兰德斯写的，他现在还在世。"},{"en":"It’s a good book called The Unbound Prometheus, which was basically that. Some of the inventions that I briefly describe in your reading, the spinning jenny, etc., refer to that. Well, that kind of analysis led one to concentrate on England, where the Industrial Revolution began, and to view industrialization as being a situation of winners and losers.","zh":"有一本好书叫做《解放的普罗米修斯》基本上就是这样的。 我在你们的阅读材料中简要描述的一些发明，比如詹妮纺纱机，都与此有关。 这种分析让我们把注意力集中在工业革命开始的英国，并把工业化看作是一种赢家和输家的局面。"},{"en":"That analysis has been rejected greatly over the past years, because the Industrial Revolution is measured by more than simply large factories with industrial workers and the number of machines. This is the point of the beginning of this. The more that we look at the Industrial Revolution, the more we see that the Industrial Revolution was first and foremost an intensification of forms of production, of kinds of production that was already there.","zh":"这种分析在过去几年里遭到了极大的驳斥，因为衡量工业革命的不仅仅是拥有产业工人的大型工厂和机器的数量。 这是这一切的开始。 我们对工业革命研究得越多，就越能发现工业革命首先是一种生产形式的集约化，一种已经存在的生产形式。"},{"en":"Thus, we spend more time looking at the intensification of artisanal production, craft production, domestic industry — which we’ve already mentioned, that is, people, mostly women but also men and children, too, working in the countryside. The rapid rise of industrial production was very much tied to traditional forms of production.","zh":"因此，我们会花更多的时间来研究手工业生产的集约化，手工业生产，家庭工业，我们已经提到过，也就是人，大部分是妇女，但也有男人和孩子，在农村工作。 工业生产的迅速崛起与传统生产形式密切相关。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S042":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"\"The first inhabitants in Australia were the ancestors of the present indigenous people. Whether these first migrations involved one or several successive waves and distinct peoples is still subject to academic debate, as is its timing. The minimum widely accepted time frame places presence of humans in Australia at 40,000 to 43,000 years Before Present, while the upper range supported by others is 60,000 to 70,000 years BP.","zh":"澳大利亚的第一批居民是现在土著居民的祖先。 这些第一批移民是涉及一波还是几波连续的浪潮，涉及不同的民族，学术界仍在争论，其时间也是如此。 被广泛接受的最小时间框架是人类出现在澳大利亚的时间比现在早4万到4.3万年，而其他学者所支持的上限范围为公元前6万\\~ 7万年。"},{"en":"In any event, this migration was achieved during the closing stages of the Pleistocene epoch, when sea levels were typically much lower than they are today. Repeated episodes of extended glaciation resulted in decreases of sea levels by some 100150 m. The continental coastline therefore extended much further out into the Timor Sea than it does today, and Australia and New Guinea formed a single landmass (known as Sahul), connected by an extensive land bridge across the Arafura Sea, Gulf of Carpentaria and Torres Strait.","zh":"无论如何，这种迁移是在更新世末期完成的，当时的海平面通常比现在要低得多。 持续的冰川作用导致海平面下降了约100150米。 因此大陆海岸线向帝汶海延伸的距离比现在要远得多，澳大利亚和新几内亚形成了一块单一的陆地(被称为萨胡尔)，由横跨阿拉弗拉海、卡彭塔利亚湾和托雷斯海峡的广阔的大陆桥连接"},{"en":"The ancestral Australian Aboriginal peoples were thus long established and continued to develop, diversify and settle through much of the continent. As the sea levels again rose at the terminus of the most recent glacial period some 10,000 years ago the Australian continent once more became a separated landmass. However, the newly formed 150 km wide Torres Strait with its chain of islands still provided the means for cultural contact and trade between New Guinea and the northern Cape York Peninsula.","zh":"澳大利亚土著的先祖因此长期建立和继续发展，多样化和定居在大陆的大部分地区。 大约一万年前，随着海平面在最近一次冰河期的终点再次上升，澳大利亚大陆再次成为一个独立的大陆块。 然而，新形成的150公里宽的托雷斯海峡及其岛链仍然为新几内亚和约克角半岛之间的文化接触和贸易提供了手段。"},{"en":"During the 1970s and 1980s around 120,000 southern Asian refugees migrated to Australia. During that twenty years, Australia first began to adopt a policy of what Minister of Immigration Al Grassby termed \"multiculturalism\". In 2004-05, Australia accepted 123,000 new settlers, a 40% increase over the past 10 years. The largest number of immigrants (40,000 in 2004-05) moved to Sydney.","zh":"在20世纪70年代和80年代，大约有12万南亚难民移民到澳大利亚。 在这二十年中，澳大利亚首次开始采用移民部长格拉斯比所称的多元文化主义政策。 2004-05年，澳大利亚接纳了12.3万名新移民，比过去10年增加了40%。"},{"en":"The majority of immigrants came from Asia, led by China and India.\"","zh":"大多数移民来自亚洲，以中国和印度为首。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S046":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Leadership can be understood as a spectrum, encompassing two primary forms: leading from the front and contributing behind the scenes. Historically, men have dominated the more visible, front-facing leadership roles, often viewed as the traditional definition of leadership. Women, on the other hand, have frequently worked behind the scenes, offering essential support, guidance, and decision-making, though often without the recognition they deserved.","zh":"领导力可以被理解为一个光谱，涵盖两种主要形式：从前方领导和在幕后贡献。 历史上，男性通常占据了更为显眼的、面向前台的领导角色，这些角色往往被视为传统意义上的领导定义。 而女性则更多地在幕后工作，提供关键支持、指导和决策，但她们的贡献往往未能得到应有的认可。"},{"en":"This dynamic reflected societal expectations and cultural norms of the time. In recent years, however, this paradigm has begun to shift significantly. Women are increasingly stepping into prominent leadership positions, breaking barriers and redefining what it means to lead. From politics and business to science and education, women are not only leading from the front but are also bringing new perspectives, collaboration, and empathy into leadership practices.","zh":"这种动态反映了当时的社会期待和文化规范。 然而，近年来，这一范式正在显著转变。 女性正越来越多地进入显著的领导岗位，打破障碍，并重新定义领导的意义。 无论是政治、商业，还是科学与教育，女性不仅在前台领导，也将新的视角、协作精神和共情融入到领导实践中。"},{"en":"This evolution underscores the importance of diverse leadership styles, demonstrating that progress is best achieved when all voices are represented. As we embrace this change, it’s clear that the future of leadership will be more inclusive and dynamic, benefiting from the strengths and contributions of everyone.","zh":"这一演变突显了多样化领导风格的重要性，表明当所有声音都得到代表时，进步才能更好地实现。 随着我们拥抱这种变化，很明显，未来的领导力将更加包容和多元化，从每个人的优势和贡献中获益。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S120":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"During this period of time, there was a huge surge of activism taking place to reverse this discrimination and injustice. Activists worked together and used non-violent protest and specific acts of targeted civil disobedience, such as the Montgomery Bus Boycott and the Greensboro Woolworth Sit-Ins, in order to bring about change. Much of this organizing and activism took place in the Southern part of the United States;","zh":"在这段时间里，出现了一股巨大的行动主义浪潮来扭转这种歧视和不公。 活动家们齐心协力，通过非暴力抗议和特定的有针对性的公民不服从行为，如蒙哥马利巴士抵制运动和格林斯博罗·伍尔沃斯静坐，来带来改变。 这些组织和行动大多发生在美国南部;"},{"en":"however, people from all over the country—of all races and religions—joined activists to proclaim their support and commitment to freedom and equality. For example, on August 28, 1963, 250,000 Americans came to Washington, D.C. for the March on Washington for Jobs and Freedom. They came to have their voices heard and listen to speeches by many civil rights leaders, especially Martin Luther King, Jr., who delivered what would become one of the most influential speeches in history.","zh":"然而，来自全国各地的人们——所有种族和宗教——加入活动人士的行列，宣布他们对自由和平等的支持和承诺。 例如，1963年8月28日，25万美国人来到华盛顿特区参加争取工作与自由的华盛顿大游行。 他们来倾听和表达自己的声音，聆听许多民权领袖的演讲，尤其是马丁·路德·金，他发表了后来成为历史上最具影响力的演讲之一。"},{"en":"In the aftermath of World War II, African American civil rights efforts were hampered by ideological splits. The Southern system of white supremacy was accompanied by the expansion of European and American imperial control over nonwhite people in Africa and Asia as well as in island countries of the Pacific and Caribbean regions. Like African Americans, most nonwhite people throughout the world were colonized or economically exploited and denied basic rights, such as the right to vote.","zh":"第二次世界大战结束后，非裔美国人的民权努力受到意识形态分歧的阻碍。 南方的白人至上制度伴随着欧洲和美国帝国对非洲、亚洲以及太平洋和加勒比地区岛国的非白人的控制扩张。 和非洲裔美国人一样，世界各地的大多数非白人都受到殖民或经济剥削，被剥夺了选举权等基本权利。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S023":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"The rise of the Internet has profoundly transformed journalism, reshaping both its production and consumption. Initially, the transition was gradual, and it took time for people to fully recognize and embrace these changes. One significant impact is the acceleration of news dissemination. The Internet has made it possible for news to spread almost instantaneously, allowing audiences to stay informed in real-time.","zh":"互联网的兴起深刻地改变了新闻业，重塑了其生产方式和消费方式。 最初，这一转变是渐进的，人们花了一段时间才完全认识到并接受这些变化。 一个显著的影响是新闻传播速度的加快。 互联网使新闻几乎可以瞬间传播，让受众能够实时获取信息。"},{"en":"Additionally, it has diversified the ways people access information, offering platforms beyond traditional newspapers and broadcasts, such as social media, blogs, and independent news sites. A particularly notable development is the emergence of new forms of journalism. Ordinary videos captured by individuals can now serve as powerful storytelling tools, often drawing attention to events that might have been overlooked by mainstream media.","zh":"此外，它还多样化了人们获取信息的方式，提供了除传统报纸和广播之外的平台，如社交媒体、博客和独立新闻网站。 一个特别值得注意的发展是新型新闻形式的出现。 普通人拍摄的视频如今可以成为强大的叙事工具，往往能够引起对主流媒体可能忽略事件的关注。"},{"en":"This democratization of journalism has expanded its reach and inclusivity, enabling more voices to participate in the global conversation. In this evolving landscape, the Internet continues to redefine journalism, fostering both opportunities and challenges for the industry.","zh":"这种新闻民主化扩大了其覆盖范围和包容性，使更多的声音能够参与全球对话。 在这一不断变化的环境中，互联网继续重新定义新闻业，为行业带来机遇与挑战。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S031":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"The rapid expansion of the Internet has revolutionized our lives, influencing both the quality and quantity of interactions and information accessibility. One significant change is in the realm of research. Online research offers several advantages, such as speed, cost-efficiency, and the ability to reach diverse or otherwise inaccessible groups.","zh":"互联网的快速扩展彻底改变了我们的生活，影响了互动的质量和数量以及信息的可获取性。 一个显著的变化出现在研究领域。 在线研究提供了诸多优势，如速度、成本效益以及能够接触到多样化或难以接触的群体。"},{"en":"These features have made it a cornerstone of modern studies and data collection, enabling researchers to gather vast amounts of information quickly. However, this shift to online methods is not without challenges. One major drawback is the lack of face-to-face communication, which eliminates the ability to interpret body language or other non-verbal cues that are essential for understanding context and intent.","zh":"这些特点使其成为现代研究和数据收集的基石，使研究人员能够迅速收集大量信息。 然而，这种转向在线方法并非没有挑战。 一个主要的缺点是缺乏面对面的沟通，这使得无法解读肢体语言或其他非语言线索，而这些对于理解背景和意图至关重要。"},{"en":"Additionally, the anonymity of the Internet means researchers cannot always verify the identity of participants, leading to potential issues with data reliability and authenticity. As online research continues to grow, balancing its advantages with strategies to mitigate its shortcomings will be crucial for maintaining the quality and credibility of studies conducted in the digital age.","zh":"此外，互联网的匿名性意味着研究人员并不总是能验证参与者的身份，从而可能引发数据可靠性和真实性的问题。 随着在线研究的持续增长，平衡其优势与采取措施缓解其缺点，对于保持数字时代研究质量和可信度至关重要。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S032":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"English, as you have already read, is not a pure language. I don’t think there really are any pure languages in the world. But English is definitely not a pure language. English, in fact, has borrowed from over 350 languages in its history. So it's a variety of many languages。","zh":"正如你已经读过的，英语不是一种纯粹的语言。 我不认为世界上有任何纯粹的语言。 但英语绝对不是一种纯粹的语言。 事实上，英语在其发展历史上借鉴了350多种语言。 所以它是多种语言的集合。"},{"en":"Some people say it’s like a dog, a mongrel dog, a dog that has been made up of many different dogs. The English language is like that. By looking at the history of the English language we learn about the history of the English people.","zh":"有些人说它就像一条狗，一条杂种狗，一条由许多不同的狗组成的狗。 英语就是这样。 通过学习英语的历史，我们可以了解英国人的历史。"},{"en":"The two things are closely connected. So, in fact, today we are not only learning about language but we are learning about history. The fact that English has borrowed words from over 350 languages has been viewed differently throughout history. So for example in Shakespeare’s time people were very angry about words which were not, they thought, original English words – words which came from other languages, they didn’t like them.","zh":"这两件事紧密相连。 所以，事实上，今天我们不仅学习语言，我们也学习历史。 纵观历史，人们对英语从350多种语言中借用词汇的看法各不相同。 例如，在莎士比亚时代，人们对那些他们认为不是原始英语的单词——来自其他语言的单词——非常愤怒，他们不喜欢它们。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S041":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Organization studies seem to draw on the whole family of social sciences, clearly psychology, clearly sociology, but also economics, anthropology, politics, as we said, philosophy to a degree, history, sometimes literary studies, cultural studies, so on and so forth. I think that's absolutely right. And for me, that's absolutely the pleasure and even on good days, the joy of doing organization studies, because it enables you not just enables, but requires you in some sense, to have some kind of broad familiarization of that sort.","zh":"组织研究似乎借鉴了整个社会科学家族的知识领域，显然包括心理学、社会学，也涉及经济学、人类学、政治学，正如我们提到的，还包括一定程度的哲学、历史学，有时甚至还有文学研究和文化研究等等。 我认为这种说法完全正确。"},{"en":"Now, there's a price to be paid for that because that kind of breadth, if you like, does come, I suppose as the cost of depth. And I guess there would be people who are clearly within academic disciplines or sociology or economics or whatever, who might say, well, these are sort of Magpie-sh, amateurish kind of forays into our territory. You know, I wouldn't necessarily disown that idea. But I think that what studying organizations teaches us and teaches me is actually the artificiality of those academic subdivisions.","zh":"当然，这样做也要付出代价，因为这种广度在某种意义上是以深度为代价的。 我想，在学术界内部，比如社会学或经济学等学科中，肯定有人会认为这种研究只是一些外行的、像喜鹊拾取般的尝试，对他们的领域而言过于肤浅。 我并不会完全否认这种说法，但我认为，组织研究真正教会我们、也教会了我的是：那些学科划分本身其实是人为的。"},{"en":"And as soon as we start to actually think about something like the organized world, then immediately, the kinds of things that come into focus are things have traditionally been studied by different demands. And so, I think it's a liberating idea, the idea that we don't need to be bound by those strictures and structures of disciplinary division, and that we can be free actually to imagine and think about the social world through an agglomeration of techniques and ideas and theories and concepts from across the social sciences.","zh":"一旦我们开始真正去思考像“组织化的世界”这样的议题，我们马上会发现，所涉及的内容往往是不同学科传统上分别研究的对象。 因此，我认为这种跨越学科界限的思维方式本身是一种解放。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S047":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Social skills are vital in enabling an individual to have and maintain positive interactions with others. Many of these skills are crucial in making and sustaining friendships. Social interactions do not always run smoothly, and an individual needs to be able to implement appropriate strategies, such as conflict resolution, when difficulties in interactions arise.","zh":"社交技能对个人能够拥有和维持与他人的积极互动至关重要。 这些技能在建立和维持友谊方面尤为重要。 社交互动并不总是顺利进行，当互动中出现困难时，个人需要能够采取适当的策略，如冲突解决。"},{"en":"It is also important for individuals to have empathy, as it allows them to respond in an understanding and caring way to how others are feeling. Children are facing social difficulties with particular risks. Young people who do not have strong relationships with the adults in their family are even more at risk. In an experiment in a high school, which lasted for 8 to 12 weeks, the students were told to be a movie director and to choose their own story structure.","zh":"同理心对于个体来说也很重要，因为它使他们能够以理解和关怀的方式回应他人的感受。 孩子们面临着特别的社交困难，尤其是那些与家庭中成年人关系不牢固的年轻人更容易受到影响。 在一项持续了8到12周的高中实验中，学生们被要求扮演电影导演的角色，选择自己的故事结构。"},{"en":"The students worked with each other, which involved lots of different skills and social interactivity. The movies they had made were actually cool. Then, the researchers tested the intervention effect, finding this can improve their self-regulation, and they found this can improve their self-regulation and critical thinking skills.","zh":"学生们相互合作，过程中涉及了许多不同的技能和社交互动。 他们制作的电影非常酷。 随后，研究人员测试了干预效果，发现这种方式可以提高学生的自我调节能力和批判性思维技能。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S048":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Today, poetry means an important part of art and culture. We often talk about the knowledge about the literature in poems. Poetry is from the oldest form of literature, probably predates the origin of writing itself. The oldest written manuscripts we have are poems. Mostly epic poems tell the stories of ancient mythology.","zh":"今天，诗歌是艺术和文化的重要组成部分。 我们经常在诗中谈论文学知识。 诗歌是最古老的文学形式，可能比写作本身的起源还要早。 我们拥有的最古老的书面手稿是诗歌。 史诗大多讲述古代神话故事。"},{"en":"The English language in poems and poetry is difficult to understand, often giving readers a feeling of frustration, making it hard for readers to enjoy poetry. This is because poems use literary expressions. Poetry was once written according to fairly strict rules of meter and rhyme, and each culture has its own rule.","zh":"诗歌中的英语语言晦涩难懂，常常给读者一种挫败感，使读者难以欣赏诗歌。 这是因为诗歌使用了文学表达。 诗歌曾经是按照相当严格的格律来写的，每种文化都有自己的规则。"},{"en":"Some poems incorporate rhyme schemes with two or more lines that end in like-sounding words. You should learn to simply enjoy it to know more about literature knowledge.","zh":"有些诗歌采用两行或两行以上的押韵方式，以发音相似的词结尾。 你应该学会简单地享受它来了解更多的文学知识。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S049":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Today, I'm going to talk to young researchers about rejection and what it takes to successfully publish your paper. As we all know, the chances of a paper being published are getting smaller and smaller, and many researchers, especially young researchers, are faced with rejection of their papers every day. Many people find that their confidence has been destroyed once their articles are rejected.","zh":"今天，我将和年轻的研究人员谈谈拒绝和成功发表论文需要什么。 我们都知道，一篇论文被发表的机会越来越小，很多研究人员，尤其是年轻的研究人员，每天都面临着论文被拒的问题。 许多人发现，一旦他们的文章被拒绝，他们的信心就被摧毁了。"},{"en":"However, having your papers rejected could actually be better for your research and even for your career path. Here, I would like to appeal to young researchers to be more positive facing rejections of your paper. We also need to think about how to attract young researchers and how to make them more involved in academic research.","zh":"然而，你的论文被拒实际上对你的研究，甚至对你的职业道路都有好处。 在这里，我想呼吁年轻的研究人员面对你的论文被拒时更加积极。 我们还需要考虑如何吸引年轻的研究人员，如何让他们更多地参与学术研究。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S053":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"A hook plays a critical role in writing a persuasive essay because it is designed to immediately capture the reader’s attention and draw them into the discussion of a controversial issue. Typically placed in the opening paragraph, a hook should consist of about four to five sentences that set the tone for the rest of the essay. The purpose is not just to introduce the topic, but to provoke the reader’s curiosity and emotional interest, encouraging them to continue reading.","zh":"引言在写作说服性文章中起着至关重要的作用，因为它的目的就是要立即抓住读者的注意力，并将他们引入到对一个有争议问题的讨论中。 通常，引言会放在开头段落里，一般由四到五句话组成，用来为整篇文章定下基调。 它的目的不仅仅是介绍话题，而是要激发读者的好奇心和情感兴趣，从而促使他们继续阅读。"},{"en":"To achieve this, writers often rely on striking statistics and verifiable facts, vivid hypothetical or worst-case scenarios, and strong, impactful wording to highlight the urgency and importance of the issue being addressed. A well-crafted hook can make the difference between a disengaged reader and one who is compelled to think more deeply about the argument that follows.","zh":"为了达到这一效果，作者往往会引用醒目的统计数据和可验证的事实，描绘生动的假设场景或最坏情况，并使用有力而富有冲击力的词语来凸显问题的紧迫性和重要性。 一个精心设计的引言，可能就是区分一个冷漠读者和一个被迫深入思考后续论点的读者的关键。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S054":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"My lectures are going to presume no special knowledge on your part. I see this as a course that's an introduction to the literature of a period, to modern poetry. We'll be studying several poets in some detail. The presumption is that they all reward and demand a certain amount of close reading.","zh":"我的讲座不会假设你们有任何特别的背景知识。 我把这门课程定位为对一个文学时期、尤其是现代诗歌的入门介绍。 我们将对几位诗人的作品进行细致深入的学习。 我相信，他们的作品不仅值得细读，也需要细读。"},{"en":"At the same time, I do mean to give you some sense of the period in which they're writing, some sense of modernism as a field, as one of the richest fields in English language writing. Finally, though, this really is a course in poetry, plain and simple. I mean to introduce you to particular poems, to give you ways to possess them, enjoy them, be puzzled or frustrated by them too;","zh":"与此同时，我也希望帮助大家了解这些诗人所处的时代背景，了解现代主义这一在英语文学中极为丰富的重要领域。 不过归根到底，这门课就是一门纯粹的诗歌课程。 我的目标是向你们介绍具体的诗歌作品，教你们掌握它们、欣赏它们，也可能会困惑或受挫；"},{"en":"to learn something from them and to care about them and to carry them with you as you go forward after this class.","zh":"希望你们能从中有所收获，真正关心这些作品，并在课程结束后仍然将它们留存在心中。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S015":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Ever try to get a baby to smile? It can seem close to impossible—and then suddenly there it is: that elusive, seemingly joyous grin. Well it turns out those smiles aren’t spontaneous—they’re strategic. Researchers have found that when babies smile, it's for a reason. They want whoever they’re interacting with—typically a parent—to smile back.","zh":"你有试过让婴儿微笑吗? 当它看起来几乎是不可能实现的时候——它就突然出现了:那难以捉摸的，看似无忧无虑的笑容。 然而事实证明，这些微笑不是自发的，而是有策略的。 研究人员发现，婴儿笑是有原因的。 他们想要和他们互动的人——通常是父母——报以微笑。"},{"en":"And they time it just so, a smile here and a smile there. The researchers call it sophisticated timing. The study is in the journal PLoS ONE. The researchers enlisted real mothers and infants and quantified their interactions, which fell into four categories. One: babies wanted to maximize the amount of time smiling at their mothers.","zh":"他们心里计算着时间，这时微笑，那时微笑。 研究人员称其为及其精密的的时间点。 这项研究发表在《公共科学图书馆·综合》杂志上。 研究人员招募了真实的母亲和婴儿，并量化了他们之间的互动，总共分为四类。 第一:婴儿想要尽可能多地对母亲微笑。"},{"en":"Two: they wanted to maximize the time the mothers smiled at them. Three: they wanted to experience simultaneous smiling, and four: no smiling at all. By studying when smiles happened and what the subsequent effect was, the investigators were able to figure out that for mothers the goal 70 percent of the time was to be smiling simultaneously—while for babies 80 percent of the time they just wanted their mother smiling at them.","zh":"二:他们想要最大限度地延长妈妈们对他们微笑的时间。 第三，他们想感受同时微笑；第四，根本不笑。 通过研究微笑发生的时间和后继的影响，研究人员能够弄清楚，对于母亲来说，70%的目标是同时微笑，而对于婴儿来说，80%的目标是只希望母亲对他们微笑。"},{"en":"So, mothers want the interaction, while babies just want to be smiled at. So your baby may not be able to feed itself, talk or even turn over yet. But when it comes to smiles, babies seem to know exactly what they're up to.","zh":"所以，妈妈们想要互动，而婴儿们只想要妈妈对自己微笑。 所以你的宝宝可能还不能自己吃饭，说话，甚至翻身。 但说到微笑，婴儿似乎很清楚自己在做什么。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"原文与翻译来自萤火虫文档（未经逐字原音核验）。"},"S021":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"The word \"need\" can be understood and used in various ways depending on the context. For example, when someone says, \"I need a holiday,\" it conveys a strong desire or preference rather than an essential requirement. This usage reflects a more subjective interpretation of the term, focusing on personal wants.","zh":"“需求”一词可以根据上下文以多种方式理解和使用。 例如，当有人说“我需要度假”时，这传达了一种强烈的渴望或偏好，而不是必不可少的要求。 这种用法反映了该词更主观的解释，侧重于个人的愿望。"},{"en":"In contrast, when you hear, \"The plant needs water,\" it is an objective statement that emphasizes necessity. Water, along with sunlight, is crucial for a plant's survival, making it a fundamental need rather than an optional desire. Additionally, the term \"need\" has psychological implications, often referring to a sense of deficiency or lack.","zh":"相反，当你听到“植物需要水”时，这是一个强调必要性的客观陈述。 水和阳光对于植物的生存至关重要，这使它成为一种基本需求，而非可有可无的愿望。 此外，“需求”一词在心理层面上也具有含义，通常指一种缺乏或不足的感觉。"},{"en":"For instance, it can describe an emotional or mental state where an individual feels incomplete or unfulfilled due to the absence of something important to their well-being. These varied usages demonstrate how the word \"need\" can span a spectrum from essential requirements to subjective desires.","zh":"例如，它可以描述一种情感或心理状态，在这种状态下，由于缺乏某些对身心健康重要的事物，个体感到不完整或不满足。 这些不同的用法表明，“需求”这个词的涵义可以从基本需求扩展到主观愿望。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S036":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Negativity bias refers to the psychological phenomenon where humans tend to focus more on negative emotions or experiences than positive ones. Although we experience positive emotions like contentment and pleasure more frequently, these feelings tend to be lighter in intensity and are less likely to be remembered or linger in our minds. On the other hand, negative emotions such as fear, anger, or sadness, although less frequent, tend to be much stronger and more intense, making them easier to recall and harder to forget.","zh":"负面偏见是指人类倾向于比积极情绪或经历更多地关注负面情绪的心理现象。 尽管我们更频繁地体验如满足和愉快等积极情绪，但这些情绪通常较轻微，不容易被记住或长时间停留在我们的脑海中。 另一方面，负面情绪，如恐惧、愤怒或悲伤，虽然较少发生，却通常更强烈，更容易回忆且更难忘记。"},{"en":"This bias has evolutionary significance. In the past, paying more attention to negative events like threats or dangers would have been advantageous for survival. By being more sensitive to potential threats—whether from predators, environmental hazards, or social conflicts—humans could respond quickly to life-threatening situations. This heightened awareness of negative stimuli would have helped our ancestors make decisions that favored safety and survival.","zh":"这种偏见具有进化意义。 通过对潜在威胁（无论是来自掠食者、环境危害还是社会冲突）更加敏感，人类可以迅速应对威胁生命的情况。 这种对负面刺激的高度敏感有助于我们的祖先做出有利于安全和生存的决策。"},{"en":"In today's world, while the immediate life-threatening threats may have diminished, the negativity bias still plays a role in how we assess situations, sometimes leading us to focus on potential risks or problems rather than opportunities or positive outcomes. Understanding this bias can help us manage our reactions and potentially shift our focus towards a more balanced perspective.","zh":"在今天的世界，虽然直接的威胁可能已减少，负面偏见仍然影响我们如何评估情况，有时让我们更多关注潜在的风险或问题，而不是机会或积极结果。 理解这种偏见可以帮助我们管理反应，并有可能将我们的焦点转向更加平衡的视角。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S045":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Far more than we're inclined to accept and sometimes even realize we are creatures of mood, that is our sense of our value as human beings is prone to extraordinary fluctuation at times. We know how to tolerate ourselves. The future seems benevolent. We can bear who we are in the eyes of others, and we can forgive ourselves for the desperate errors of the past.","zh":"远比我们倾向于接受，有时甚至意识到我们是情绪的生物，那就是我们的价值感，作为人类，有时容易发生巨大的波动。 我们知道如何容忍自己。 未来似乎是仁慈的。 我们能忍受别人眼中的自己，我们能原谅自己过去犯下的绝望的错误。"},{"en":"And then at other points, the mood dips and we lament most of what we've ever done. We see ourselves as natural targets for contempt. We feel undeserving, guilty, weak and headed for retribution and disaster. But it can be very hard to grasp what causes our moods to shift.","zh":"而在其他时候，我们的情绪会下降，我们会为我们做过的大多数事情感到悲伤。 我们认为自己天生就是被鄙视的对象。 我们感到不配，内疚，软弱，走向报复和灾难。 但是很难理解是什么原因导致我们的情绪变化。"},{"en":"A day that started with energy and hope can by lunchtime end up mired in self-hatred and tearfulness. A sure sense that we finally turned the corner and are on the way to better things can be replaced at speed by an alternative certainty that we are a cosmic error. We cannot, it appears, ever prevent our moods from being subject to change.","zh":"充满活力和希望的一天，到午餐时间就会陷入自我憎恨和泪流满面。 我们终于渡过了难关，踏上了通往更好事物的道路，这种肯定的感觉很快就会被另一种肯定所取代，那就是我们是一个宇宙错误。 我们似乎永远无法阻止情绪的变化。"},{"en":"But what is open to us all is to learn how to manage the change more effectively so that our downturn's can be ever so slightly more gentle or sadness more containable, and our inconstancy less shameful in our eyes.","zh":"但对我们所有人开放的是学习如何更有效地管理这种变化，这样我们的低迷就会稍微温和一些，悲伤就会更可控一些，我们的反复无常在我们眼里就不会那么可耻了。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"},"S119":{"paragraphs":[{"en":"Approach motivation and avoidance motivation are two fundamental types of motivation that drive human behavior in different ways. Approach motivation refers to the desire to move toward positive outcomes or rewards, such as achieving a career goal, securing a promotion, or planning a rewarding vacation. This type of motivation is typically linked to long-term aspirations and personal growth, as people are driven by the possibility of gaining something valuable.","zh":"接近动机和回避动机是驱动人类行为的两种基本动机，它们以不同的方式影响我们的行为。 接近动机指的是渴望朝向积极结果或奖励前进的动力，比如实现职业目标、获得晋升或规划一次有意义的假期。 这种动机通常与长期愿望和个人成长相关，因为人们被获得某些有价值的东西的可能性所驱动。"},{"en":"It encourages individuals to take action, make progress, and pursue opportunities that lead to success or happiness. In contrast, avoidance motivation involves the drive to move away from negative outcomes or unpleasant situations. For example, someone may work hard to avoid failure, rejection, or criticism, or may take steps to prevent an undesirable situation, such as a stressful meeting or a confrontation.","zh":"它鼓励个人采取行动、取得进展，并追求能够带来成功或幸福的机会。 相反，回避动机涉及避免负面结果或不愉快情境的驱动力。 例如，有人可能会努力工作以避免失败、拒绝或批评，或者采取措施以避免不愿面对的情境，如压力大的会议或冲突。"},{"en":"The goal here is not to achieve something positive, but rather to avoid something negative, often in an effort to reduce anxiety, fear, or discomfort. While both types of motivation play a role in shaping human behavior, avoidance motivation tends to have a stronger emotional impact. This is because it is often more immediate and urgent in nature.","zh":"这里的目标不是追求某种积极的东西，而是避免某种负面的东西，通常是为了减少焦虑、恐惧或不适。 虽然这两种动机都在塑造人类行为中发挥作用，但回避动机往往具有更强的情感影响。 这是因为回避动机通常更为直接且紧迫。"},{"en":"People tend to be more strongly motivated by the need to avoid pain, stress, or negative emotions than by the pursuit of rewards or pleasure. As a result, avoidance motivation can lead to quicker, more reactive decision-making, while approach motivation often leads to more calculated, long-term planning. Both types of motivation are crucial in different contexts, and understanding the balance between them can help individuals better navigate challenges and opportunities in both their personal and professional lives.","zh":"人们通常更强烈地被避免痛苦、压力或负面情绪的需求所驱动，而不是追求奖励或愉悦。 因此，回避动机可能导致更快速、更具反应性的决策，而接近动机则通常导致更为谨慎、长期的规划。 这两种动机在不同的情境中都至关重要，理解它们之间的平衡可以帮助个人在个人生活和职业生涯中更好地应对挑战和机遇。"}],"status":"firefly_reference","note":"萤火虫资料标注：非真实音频。以下为网站提供的参考文本，不保证与当前音频逐字相同。"}};
